0, 295, 257, 5507, 11, 10024, 4103, 445, 402, 37690, 2584, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11780322900339335, "compression_ratio": 1.7263513513513513, "no_speech_prob": 8.100748262289403e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 3000, "start": 46.019999999999996, "end": 46.68, "text": " Totally shatters.", "tokens": [51166, 22837, 402, 37690, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11780322900339335, "compression_ratio": 1.7263513513513513, "no_speech_prob": 8.100748262289403e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 3000, "start": 46.8, "end": 54.5, "text": " What is happening on that stage is actually this elaborate, beautifully coordinated acoustic illusion.", "tokens": [51205, 708, 307, 2737, 322, 300, 3233, 307, 767, 341, 20945, 11, 16525, 29591, 26753, 18854, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11780322900339335, "compression_ratio": 1.7263513513513513, "no_speech_prob": 8.100748262289403e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 3000, "start": 54.8, "end": 59.980000000000004, "text": " It is entirely an illusion, and, I mean, what's fascinating here is that the musicians aren't being tricked.", "tokens": [51605, 467, 307, 7696, 364, 18854, 11, 293, 11, 286, 914, 11, 437, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 300, 264, 16916, 3212, 380, 885, 39345, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11780322900339335, "compression_ratio": 1.7263513513513513, "no_speech_prob": 8.100748262289403e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 6000, "start": 60.0, "end": 63.58, "text": " You know, they are actively weaponizing it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 458, 11, 436, 366, 13022, 7463, 3319, 309, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 6000, "start": 63.92, "end": 69.84, "text": " The architecture of that illusion is profoundly important, and not just for, like, audio engineers.", "tokens": [50561, 440, 9482, 295, 300, 18854, 307, 39954, 1021, 11, 293, 406, 445, 337, 11, 411, 11, 6278, 11955, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 6000, "start": 69.96000000000001, "end": 73.36, "text": " It's important for anyone trying to build complex systems in the real world.", "tokens": [50863, 467, 311, 1021, 337, 2878, 1382, 281, 1322, 3997, 3652, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 6000, "start": 73.7, "end": 75.44, "text": " Well, welcome to the deep dive.", "tokens": [51050, 1042, 11, 2928, 281, 264, 2452, 9192, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 6000, "start": 75.74, "end": 79.18, "text": " We are taking you straight to the core of a massive idea today.", "tokens": [51152, 492, 366, 1940, 291, 2997, 281, 264, 4965, 295, 257, 5994, 1558, 965, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 6000, "start": 79.28, "end": 79.82, "text": " You really are.", "tokens": [51329, 509, 534, 366, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 6000, "start": 80.16, "end": 84.2, "text": " Our mission is to shortcut the path to being genuinely well-informed.", "tokens": [51373, 2621, 4447, 307, 281, 24822, 264, 3100, 281, 885, 17839, 731, 12, 259, 22892, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1583190389198832, "compression_ratio": 1.576470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 8420, "start": 84.2, "end": 89.3, "text": " We want to strip away the noise so you can grasp the actual mechanics of how things work.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 528, 281, 12828, 1314, 264, 5658, 370, 291, 393, 21743, 264, 3539, 12939, 295, 577, 721, 589, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 8420, "start": 90.42, "end": 94.62, "text": " So today we're looking at this brilliant piece of writing from August 2026.", "tokens": [50676, 407, 965, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 341, 10248, 2522, 295, 3579, 490, 6897, 945, 10880, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 8420, "start": 94.76, "end": 102.56, "text": " It's by the essayist Fliction, and it's titled Hall of Monitors, Coordination Without Identical Information.", "tokens": [50893, 467, 311, 538, 264, 16238, 468, 3235, 4105, 11, 293, 309, 311, 19841, 5434, 295, 4713, 9862, 11, 3066, 765, 2486, 9129, 25905, 804, 15357, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 8420, "start": 102.76, "end": 103.66, "text": " Such a great title.", "tokens": [51293, 9653, 257, 869, 4876, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 8420, "start": 103.98, "end": 104.38, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51354, 467, 307, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 8420, "start": 104.52000000000001, "end": 107.38, "text": " And our entire conversation centers on this premise.", "tokens": [51381, 400, 527, 2302, 3761, 10898, 322, 341, 22045, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 8420, "start": 107.54, "end": 107.78, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51532, 865, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1768730084101359, "compression_ratio": 1.4754098360655739, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895796185063204e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10778, "start": 107.78, "end": 109.26, "text": " The live rock band.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1621, 3727, 4116, 13, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10778, "start": 109.92, "end": 114.36, "text": " You, standing in the audience, think you're sharing an acoustic reality with the people on stage.", "tokens": [50472, 509, 11, 4877, 294, 264, 4034, 11, 519, 291, 434, 5414, 364, 26753, 4103, 365, 264, 561, 322, 3233, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10778, "start": 114.56, "end": 122.72, "text": " Right, but what is physically happening up there, the physical reality, is that not a single person on that stage is hearing what you, the audience member, are hearing.", "tokens": [50704, 1779, 11, 457, 437, 307, 9762, 2737, 493, 456, 11, 264, 4001, 4103, 11, 307, 300, 406, 257, 2167, 954, 322, 300, 3233, 307, 4763, 437, 291, 11, 264, 4034, 4006, 11, 366, 4763, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10778, "start": 123.1, "end": 123.32000000000001, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51131, 883, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10778, "start": 123.4, "end": 129.22, "text": " Furthermore, not a single person on that stage is hearing what the musician standing, like, three feet away from them is hearing.", "tokens": [51146, 23999, 11, 406, 257, 2167, 954, 322, 300, 3233, 307, 4763, 437, 264, 19570, 4877, 11, 411, 11, 1045, 3521, 1314, 490, 552, 307, 4763, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 10778, "start": 129.5, "end": 133.04, "text": " The singer's reality is entirely divorced from the bassist's reality.", "tokens": [51451, 440, 11564, 311, 4103, 307, 7696, 27670, 490, 264, 10136, 468, 311, 4103, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11833632403406603, "compression_ratio": 1.906614785992218, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457206269468225e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 13304, "start": 133.04, "end": 137.5, "text": " The drummer's world is fundamentally different from the guitarist's world.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 38535, 311, 1002, 307, 17879, 819, 490, 264, 7531, 468, 311, 1002, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 13304, "start": 137.82, "end": 146.85999999999999, "text": " And the goal of our deep dive today is to explore why this stage engineering trick is actually a grand overarching theory.", "tokens": [50604, 400, 264, 3387, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 965, 307, 281, 6839, 983, 341, 3233, 7043, 4282, 307, 767, 257, 2697, 45501, 5261, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 13304, "start": 147.0, "end": 148.01999999999998, "text": " It's a blueprint, really.", "tokens": [51063, 467, 311, 257, 35868, 11, 534, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 13304, "start": 148.18, "end": 156.51999999999998, "text": " Yeah, a blueprint for how human beings, distributed software, social platforms, and highly complex multi-agent systems coordinate.", "tokens": [51122, 865, 11, 257, 35868, 337, 577, 1952, 8958, 11, 12631, 4722, 11, 2093, 9473, 11, 293, 5405, 3997, 4825, 12, 559, 317, 3652, 15670, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 13304, "start": 156.79999999999998, "end": 159.95999999999998, "text": " And how they do it without ever actually sharing identical information.", "tokens": [51553, 400, 577, 436, 360, 309, 1553, 1562, 767, 5414, 14800, 1589, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 13304, "start": 160.23999999999998, "end": 160.51999999999998, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51725, 1079, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350579173294538, "compression_ratio": 1.6082089552238805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368493153436469e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 16052, "start": 160.52, "end": 166.18, "text": " So setting the baseline thesis here, which affliction just deconstructs masterfully.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 3287, 264, 20518, 22288, 510, 11, 597, 2096, 75, 4105, 445, 49473, 1757, 82, 4505, 2277, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118610382080078, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546424824569582e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 16052, "start": 166.18, "end": 166.58, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [50648, 39978, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118610382080078, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546424824569582e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 16052, "start": 166.82000000000002, "end": 177.42000000000002, "text": " The thesis going into this is our inherent societal assumption that fairness or coordination or a functional shared truth absolutely requires giving everyone the exact same feed.", "tokens": [50680, 440, 22288, 516, 666, 341, 307, 527, 26387, 33472, 15302, 300, 29765, 420, 21252, 420, 257, 11745, 5507, 3494, 3122, 7029, 2902, 1518, 264, 1900, 912, 3154, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118610382080078, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546424824569582e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 16052, "start": 177.52, "end": 177.66000000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51215, 1779, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118610382080078, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546424824569582e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 16052, "start": 177.74, "end": 181.04000000000002, "text": " We assume we must all perceive the identical reality to act together.", "tokens": [51226, 492, 6552, 321, 1633, 439, 20281, 264, 14800, 4103, 281, 605, 1214, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118610382080078, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546424824569582e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 18104, "start": 181.04, "end": 181.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2225569972285518, "compression_ratio": 1.4049079754601228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977376756695638e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 18104, "start": 181.54, "end": 183.5, "text": " We think, you know, sameness equals fairness.", "tokens": [50390, 492, 519, 11, 291, 458, 11, 3247, 15264, 6915, 29765, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2225569972285518, "compression_ratio": 1.4049079754601228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977376756695638e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 18104, "start": 184.14, "end": 192.23999999999998, "text": " But this essay proves why that assumption is not just mathematically and physically wrong, but why building systems based on that assumption is actively dangerous.", "tokens": [50520, 583, 341, 16238, 25019, 983, 300, 15302, 307, 406, 445, 44003, 293, 9762, 2085, 11, 457, 983, 2390, 3652, 2361, 322, 300, 15302, 307, 13022, 5795, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2225569972285518, "compression_ratio": 1.4049079754601228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977376756695638e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 18104, "start": 192.68, "end": 193.26, "text": " It's wild.", "tokens": [50947, 467, 311, 4868, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2225569972285518, "compression_ratio": 1.4049079754601228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977376756695638e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 19326, "start": 193.26, "end": 201.54, "text": " So to truly grasp the theory, we need to completely deconstruct the physical reality of the stage that inspired it.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 281, 4908, 21743, 264, 5261, 11, 321, 643, 281, 2584, 49473, 1757, 264, 4001, 4103, 295, 264, 3233, 300, 7547, 309, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12186486533518588, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.083814457792821e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 19326, "start": 201.82, "end": 206.76, "text": " Yeah, we have to look at what is actually being piped into the in-ear monitors of these musicians.", "tokens": [50793, 865, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 437, 307, 767, 885, 8489, 292, 666, 264, 294, 12, 14881, 26518, 295, 613, 16916, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12186486533518588, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.083814457792821e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 19326, "start": 206.76, "end": 212.0, "text": " Because if you've ever watched a live performance and seen a musician, like casually adjust that little earpiece.", "tokens": [51040, 1436, 498, 291, 600, 1562, 6337, 257, 1621, 3389, 293, 1612, 257, 19570, 11, 411, 34872, 4369, 300, 707, 1273, 15281, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12186486533518588, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.083814457792821e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 19326, "start": 212.1, "end": 215.14, "text": " They are tweaking a highly curated version of reality.", "tokens": [51307, 814, 366, 6986, 2456, 257, 5405, 47851, 3037, 295, 4103, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12186486533518588, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 2.083814457792821e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 21514, "start": 215.14, "end": 215.57999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 21514, "start": 215.83999999999997, "end": 216.85999999999999, "text": " Let's start with the drummer.", "tokens": [50400, 961, 311, 722, 365, 264, 38535, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 21514, "start": 217.89999999999998, "end": 223.45999999999998, "text": " The audience is getting hit with this massive, overwhelming wall of sound.", "tokens": [50503, 440, 4034, 307, 1242, 2045, 365, 341, 5994, 11, 13373, 2929, 295, 1626, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 21514, "start": 223.98, "end": 224.14, "text": " Right?", "tokens": [50807, 1779, 30, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 21514, "start": 224.29999999999998, "end": 228.44, "text": " Screaming guitars, layered synths, crashing cymbals, five vocal harmonies.", "tokens": [50823, 2747, 38072, 36809, 11, 34666, 10657, 82, 11, 26900, 3185, 2504, 1124, 11, 1732, 11657, 14750, 530, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 21514, "start": 228.45999999999998, "end": 229.35999999999999, "text": " It's huge.", "tokens": [51031, 467, 311, 2603, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 21514, "start": 229.42, "end": 236.2, "text": " But if you were to walk up to the drummer and say, pop one of their earpieces into your own ear, what does that world sound like?", "tokens": [51079, 583, 498, 291, 645, 281, 1792, 493, 281, 264, 38535, 293, 584, 11, 1665, 472, 295, 641, 1273, 47488, 666, 428, 1065, 1273, 11, 437, 775, 300, 1002, 1626, 411, 30, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837927513934196, "compression_ratio": 1.4933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.85339395740447e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 23620, "start": 236.2, "end": 238.32, "text": " Honestly, it would sound incredibly bizarre.", "tokens": [50365, 12348, 11, 309, 576, 1626, 6252, 18265, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 23620, "start": 238.61999999999998, "end": 240.72, "text": " Like almost unrecognizable as the song you're listening to.", "tokens": [50486, 1743, 1920, 517, 13867, 2912, 22395, 382, 264, 2153, 291, 434, 4764, 281, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 23620, "start": 240.79999999999998, "end": 241.01999999999998, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [50595, 4083, 30, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 23620, "start": 241.28, "end": 241.54, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50619, 865, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 23620, "start": 241.94, "end": 252.06, "text": " The drummer is hearing mostly a highly compressed, isolated bass guitar line, the rhythmic click of a metronome, and perhaps a tiny thin thread of the lead vocal.", "tokens": [50652, 440, 38535, 307, 4763, 5240, 257, 5405, 30353, 11, 14621, 10136, 7531, 1622, 11, 264, 46967, 2052, 295, 257, 1131, 2044, 423, 11, 293, 4317, 257, 5870, 5862, 7207, 295, 264, 1477, 11657, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 23620, "start": 252.48, "end": 252.88, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51179, 3153, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 23620, "start": 252.88, "end": 259.86, "text": " They are explicitly not hearing the wash of the cymbals they're hitting, and they are definitely not hearing the rich distortion of the rhythm guitar.", "tokens": [51199, 814, 366, 20803, 406, 4763, 264, 5675, 295, 264, 3185, 2504, 1124, 436, 434, 8850, 11, 293, 436, 366, 2138, 406, 4763, 264, 4593, 28426, 295, 264, 11801, 7531, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 23620, "start": 260.24, "end": 261.14, "text": " Yeah, and why is that?", "tokens": [51567, 865, 11, 293, 983, 307, 300, 30, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14541211902585804, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302486282645853e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 26114, "start": 261.14, "end": 267.74, "text": " Because, I mean, if I'm the drummer and I hear everything, I actually can't do my job.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 11, 286, 914, 11, 498, 286, 478, 264, 38535, 293, 286, 1568, 1203, 11, 286, 767, 393, 380, 360, 452, 1691, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 26114, "start": 267.94, "end": 268.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50705, 7587, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 26114, "start": 268.47999999999996, "end": 273.14, "text": " If I hear the wash of noise the audience hears, the subtle variations in the rhythm get muddy.", "tokens": [50732, 759, 286, 1568, 264, 5675, 295, 5658, 264, 4034, 25688, 11, 264, 13743, 17840, 294, 264, 11801, 483, 38540, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 26114, "start": 273.62, "end": 274.65999999999997, "text": " I lose the groove.", "tokens": [50989, 286, 3624, 264, 26910, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 26114, "start": 274.71999999999997, "end": 275.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51044, 1779, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 26114, "start": 275.06, "end": 276.32, "text": " Your brain is just overloaded.", "tokens": [51061, 2260, 3567, 307, 445, 28777, 292, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 26114, "start": 276.34, "end": 276.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51125, 1079, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 26114, "start": 276.68, "end": 287.38, "text": " I need the bass player to anchor the temporal reality of the song, and I need just enough of the lead singer's voice to know if we're, like, entering the chorus or the bridge.", "tokens": [51142, 286, 643, 264, 10136, 4256, 281, 18487, 264, 30881, 4103, 295, 264, 2153, 11, 293, 286, 643, 445, 1547, 295, 264, 1477, 11564, 311, 3177, 281, 458, 498, 321, 434, 11, 411, 11, 11104, 264, 22632, 420, 264, 7283, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 26114, "start": 287.59999999999997, "end": 289.28, "text": " Everything else is a distraction.", "tokens": [51688, 5471, 1646, 307, 257, 30217, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 26114, "start": 289.65999999999997, "end": 290.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51791, 7587, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1590844947873181, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860264490630271e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 29012, "start": 290.12, "end": 295.08, "text": " The drummer's cognitive load is entirely dedicated to keeping time and structure.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 38535, 311, 15605, 3677, 307, 7696, 8374, 281, 5145, 565, 293, 3877, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 29012, "start": 296.08, "end": 297.9, "text": " Now, contrast that with the lead singer.", "tokens": [50663, 823, 11, 8712, 300, 365, 264, 1477, 11564, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 29012, "start": 298.28000000000003, "end": 304.14, "text": " If you listen to the singer's monitor mix, you're going to hear their own voice pushed aggressively forward.", "tokens": [50773, 759, 291, 2140, 281, 264, 11564, 311, 6002, 2890, 11, 291, 434, 516, 281, 1568, 641, 1065, 3177, 9152, 32024, 2128, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 29012, "start": 304.26, "end": 304.82, "text": " Oh, I bet.", "tokens": [51072, 876, 11, 286, 778, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 29012, "start": 305.0, "end": 314.72, "text": " It will be overwhelmingly loud and dry, sitting right at the front of their skull, and alongside that, they might have a single keyboard line or an acoustic guitar.", "tokens": [51109, 467, 486, 312, 42926, 6588, 293, 4016, 11, 3798, 558, 412, 264, 1868, 295, 641, 11743, 11, 293, 12385, 300, 11, 436, 1062, 362, 257, 2167, 10186, 1622, 420, 364, 26753, 7531, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 29012, "start": 315.04, "end": 318.94, "text": " Because the singer doesn't need the pounding, low-end frequencies of the bass and kick drum.", "tokens": [51611, 1436, 264, 11564, 1177, 380, 643, 264, 40034, 11, 2295, 12, 521, 20250, 295, 264, 10136, 293, 4437, 10206, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13217259268475395, "compression_ratio": 1.6025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693298018576216e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 31894, "start": 318.94, "end": 319.46, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29880057440863717, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251251867312576e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 31894, "start": 319.71999999999997, "end": 324.16, "text": " In fact, those frequencies will actually vibrate their vocal cords and throw off their intonation.", "tokens": [50404, 682, 1186, 11, 729, 20250, 486, 767, 11666, 4404, 641, 11657, 36302, 293, 3507, 766, 641, 560, 266, 399, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29880057440863717, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251251867312576e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 31894, "start": 324.28, "end": 324.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50632, 1779, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29880057440863717, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251251867312576e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 31894, "start": 324.71999999999997, "end": 324.96, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50654, 865, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29880057440863717, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251251867312576e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 32496, "start": 324.96, "end": 327.23999999999995, "text": " It physically interferes with their instrument.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 9762, 25799, 279, 365, 641, 7198, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 32496, "start": 327.23999999999995, "end": 329.88, "text": " So, they need a pure melodic reference.", "tokens": [50479, 407, 11, 436, 643, 257, 6075, 32834, 299, 6408, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 32496, "start": 330.38, "end": 331.28, "text": " A pitch center.", "tokens": [50636, 316, 7293, 3056, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 32496, "start": 331.62, "end": 338.0, "text": " They need to hear themselves clearly enough to not blow out their vocal cords trying to compete with the room volume.", "tokens": [50698, 814, 643, 281, 1568, 2969, 4448, 1547, 281, 406, 6327, 484, 641, 11657, 36302, 1382, 281, 11831, 365, 264, 1808, 5523, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 32496, "start": 338.15999999999997, "end": 338.59999999999997, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51025, 48746, 736, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 32496, "start": 338.94, "end": 342.74, "text": " And then you get to the most counterintuitive mix of all, which is the guitarist.", "tokens": [51064, 400, 550, 291, 483, 281, 264, 881, 5682, 686, 48314, 2890, 295, 439, 11, 597, 307, 264, 7531, 468, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18988330275924117, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758159309363974e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 34274, "start": 342.74, "end": 343.26, "text": " Oh, my gosh.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 452, 6502, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 34274, "start": 343.32, "end": 344.8, "text": " This detail blew my mind.", "tokens": [50394, 639, 2607, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 34274, "start": 344.86, "end": 345.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50471, 1779, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 34274, "start": 345.28000000000003, "end": 354.12, "text": " If you talk to a professional touring guitarist, a lot of the time, they want almost none of their own instrument in their in-ear monitor.", "tokens": [50492, 759, 291, 751, 281, 257, 4843, 32487, 7531, 468, 11, 257, 688, 295, 264, 565, 11, 436, 528, 1920, 6022, 295, 641, 1065, 7198, 294, 641, 294, 12, 14881, 6002, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 34274, "start": 354.32, "end": 355.66, "text": " Almost none of it.", "tokens": [50944, 12627, 6022, 295, 309, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 34274, "start": 355.78000000000003, "end": 357.36, "text": " Which sounds insane.", "tokens": [51017, 3013, 3263, 10838, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 34274, "start": 357.7, "end": 358.72, "text": " You're playing an instrument.", "tokens": [51113, 509, 434, 2433, 364, 7198, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 34274, "start": 359.38, "end": 361.28000000000003, "text": " Surely, you need to hear exactly what you're playing.", "tokens": [51197, 29803, 11, 291, 643, 281, 1568, 2293, 437, 291, 434, 2433, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.160563843973567, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 36128, "start": 361.28, "end": 368.82, "text": " It sounds like a mistake until you break down the physical mechanics of playing the electric guitar on a loud stage.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3263, 411, 257, 6146, 1826, 291, 1821, 760, 264, 4001, 12939, 295, 2433, 264, 5210, 7531, 322, 257, 6588, 3233, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 36128, "start": 368.91999999999996, "end": 369.58, "text": " Okay, break it down.", "tokens": [50747, 1033, 11, 1821, 309, 760, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 36128, "start": 369.97999999999996, "end": 371.71999999999997, "text": " Well, first, they already know what their hands are doing.", "tokens": [50800, 1042, 11, 700, 11, 436, 1217, 458, 437, 641, 2377, 366, 884, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 36128, "start": 371.79999999999995, "end": 372.65999999999997, "text": " They have muscle memory.", "tokens": [50891, 814, 362, 8679, 4675, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 36128, "start": 372.79999999999995, "end": 373.05999999999995, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50941, 4894, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 36128, "start": 373.21999999999997, "end": 378.09999999999997, "text": " But more importantly, they're standing in front of an amplifier pushing actual air, right?", "tokens": [50962, 583, 544, 8906, 11, 436, 434, 4877, 294, 1868, 295, 364, 27439, 7380, 3539, 1988, 11, 558, 30, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 36128, "start": 378.28, "end": 378.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51215, 1779, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 36128, "start": 378.55999999999995, "end": 382.5, "text": " So, they can physically feel the resonance of the instrument against their bottom.", "tokens": [51229, 407, 11, 436, 393, 9762, 841, 264, 30944, 295, 264, 7198, 1970, 641, 2767, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 36128, "start": 382.53999999999996, "end": 383.53999999999996, "text": " Oh, like bone conduction.", "tokens": [51428, 876, 11, 411, 9026, 43842, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 36128, "start": 383.65999999999997, "end": 383.79999999999995, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51484, 865, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12037171726733183, "compression_ratio": 1.5658362989323844, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308654951334821e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 38380, "start": 383.8, "end": 384.40000000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 38380, "start": 384.6, "end": 385.8, "text": " They have bone conduction.", "tokens": [50405, 814, 362, 9026, 43842, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 38380, "start": 386.6, "end": 391.8, "text": " So, what they desperately lack in that loud environment is spatial and temporal awareness.", "tokens": [50505, 407, 11, 437, 436, 23726, 5011, 294, 300, 6588, 2823, 307, 23598, 293, 30881, 8888, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 38380, "start": 392.14, "end": 392.8, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [50782, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 38380, "start": 392.92, "end": 400.94, "text": " They need the hi-hat of the drum kit to know exactly when to land the downbeat, and they need the vocal to know the emotional dynamic of the section.", "tokens": [50821, 814, 643, 264, 4879, 12, 15178, 295, 264, 10206, 8260, 281, 458, 2293, 562, 281, 2117, 264, 760, 4169, 11, 293, 436, 643, 264, 11657, 281, 458, 264, 6863, 8546, 295, 264, 3541, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 38380, "start": 401.16, "end": 402.48, "text": " That makes so much sense.", "tokens": [51233, 663, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 38380, "start": 402.54, "end": 408.34000000000003, "text": " If their monitor was just their own guitar, they would be a soloist completely divorced from the band.", "tokens": [51302, 759, 641, 6002, 390, 445, 641, 1065, 7531, 11, 436, 576, 312, 257, 6944, 468, 2584, 27670, 490, 264, 4116, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12034721557910626, "compression_ratio": 1.6468253968253967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493891113340207e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 40834, "start": 408.34, "end": 417.09999999999997, "text": " So, if you ask a working musician why their mix sounds absolutely nothing like the ambient room, their answer isn't that they are confused.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 291, 1029, 257, 1364, 19570, 983, 641, 2890, 3263, 3122, 1825, 411, 264, 22997, 1808, 11, 641, 1867, 1943, 380, 300, 436, 366, 9019, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 40834, "start": 417.29999999999995, "end": 417.9, "text": " No, never.", "tokens": [50813, 883, 11, 1128, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 40834, "start": 418.11999999999995, "end": 420.82, "text": " The answer is that the discrepancy is by design.", "tokens": [50854, 440, 1867, 307, 300, 264, 2983, 265, 6040, 1344, 307, 538, 1715, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 40834, "start": 421.2, "end": 428.71999999999997, "text": " That highly filtered, bizarre-sounding mix is an engineered reality constructed specifically to allow them to execute their role.", "tokens": [51008, 663, 5405, 37111, 11, 18265, 12, 82, 24625, 2890, 307, 364, 38648, 4103, 17083, 4682, 281, 2089, 552, 281, 14483, 641, 3090, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 40834, "start": 429.15999999999997, "end": 434.94, "text": " And what's fascinating here is that Flitschen makes this massive leap from audio engineering to systems architecture.", "tokens": [51406, 400, 437, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 300, 3235, 1208, 2470, 1669, 341, 5994, 19438, 490, 6278, 7043, 281, 3652, 9482, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 40834, "start": 435.05999999999995, "end": 435.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51701, 865, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 40834, "start": 435.47999999999996, "end": 436.26, "text": " This is where it gets big.", "tokens": [51722, 639, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 955, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13428330003169545, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099970106415394e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 43626, "start": 436.26, "end": 440.06, "text": " This stage setup isn't just a quirky byproduct of loud music.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 3233, 8657, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 49515, 538, 33244, 295, 6588, 1318, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09171124343033675, "compression_ratio": 1.564748201438849, "no_speech_prob": 1.707789183506836e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 43626, "start": 440.38, "end": 447.92, "text": " It is a working, highly successful example of an architecture that most systems claiming to coordinate people totally fail to build.", "tokens": [50571, 467, 307, 257, 1364, 11, 5405, 4406, 1365, 295, 364, 9482, 300, 881, 3652, 19232, 281, 15670, 561, 3879, 3061, 281, 1322, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09171124343033675, "compression_ratio": 1.564748201438849, "no_speech_prob": 1.707789183506836e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 43626, "start": 448.14, "end": 463.28, "text": " Whether we're talking about algorithmic news feeds, enterprise software used by multinational corporations, or distributed AI networks, they either fail to grasp this architecture or they actively avoid building it.", "tokens": [50959, 8503, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 9284, 299, 2583, 23712, 11, 14132, 4722, 1143, 538, 45872, 1478, 17676, 11, 420, 12631, 7318, 9590, 11, 436, 2139, 3061, 281, 21743, 341, 9482, 420, 436, 13022, 5042, 2390, 309, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09171124343033675, "compression_ratio": 1.564748201438849, "no_speech_prob": 1.707789183506836e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 43626, "start": 463.48, "end": 464.48, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [51726, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09171124343033675, "compression_ratio": 1.564748201438849, "no_speech_prob": 1.707789183506836e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 46448, "start": 464.48, "end": 468.66, "text": " I have to challenge you on the idea that tech platforms actively avoid this.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 362, 281, 3430, 291, 322, 264, 1558, 300, 7553, 9473, 13022, 5042, 341, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3043772863305133, "compression_ratio": 1.0389610389610389, "no_speech_prob": 2.676588334651897e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 46448, "start": 468.72, "end": 469.04, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [50577, 876, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3043772863305133, "compression_ratio": 1.0389610389610389, "no_speech_prob": 2.676588334651897e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 46904, "start": 469.04, "end": 474.16, "text": " Because on the surface, this sounds exactly like what Silicon Valley does every single day.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 322, 264, 3753, 11, 341, 3263, 2293, 411, 437, 25351, 10666, 775, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 46904, "start": 474.28000000000003, "end": 475.86, "text": " They personalize everything.", "tokens": [50627, 814, 2973, 1125, 1203, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 46904, "start": 475.98, "end": 476.44, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [50712, 814, 360, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 46904, "start": 476.68, "end": 480.76000000000005, "text": " My social media feed looks absolutely nothing like your social media feed.", "tokens": [50747, 1222, 2093, 3021, 3154, 1542, 3122, 1825, 411, 428, 2093, 3021, 3154, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 46904, "start": 481.0, "end": 482.72, "text": " My search results are different from yours.", "tokens": [50963, 1222, 3164, 3542, 366, 819, 490, 6342, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 46904, "start": 483.04, "end": 487.52000000000004, "text": " Isn't that the exact same thing as the drummer getting a different mix than the singer?", "tokens": [51065, 6998, 380, 300, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 382, 264, 38535, 1242, 257, 819, 2890, 813, 264, 11564, 30, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16931393207647863, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 2.3995278420479993e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 48752, "start": 487.52, "end": 489.24, "text": " It's a customized feed.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 30581, 3154, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 48752, "start": 489.24, "end": 490.7, "text": " It is customized, yes.", "tokens": [50451, 467, 307, 30581, 11, 2086, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 48752, "start": 490.9, "end": 494.5, "text": " But the mechanics underneath that customization are entirely different.", "tokens": [50534, 583, 264, 12939, 7223, 300, 39387, 366, 7696, 819, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 48752, "start": 494.64, "end": 495.0, "text": " How's that?", "tokens": [50721, 1012, 311, 300, 30, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 48752, "start": 495.24, "end": 499.82, "text": " What tech platforms are currently doing is like a dark mirror of what the band is doing.", "tokens": [50751, 708, 7553, 9473, 366, 4362, 884, 307, 411, 257, 2877, 8013, 295, 437, 264, 4116, 307, 884, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 48752, "start": 500.12, "end": 500.58, "text": " Dark mirror.", "tokens": [50995, 9563, 8013, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 48752, "start": 500.68, "end": 500.82, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51023, 865, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 48752, "start": 501.2, "end": 509.46, "text": " The band's setup, no matter how disparate the individual mixes get, strictly maintains a structural, verifiable connection to a single shared reality.", "tokens": [51049, 440, 4116, 311, 8657, 11, 572, 1871, 577, 14548, 473, 264, 2609, 37121, 483, 11, 20792, 33385, 257, 15067, 11, 1306, 30876, 4984, 281, 257, 2167, 5507, 4103, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 48752, "start": 509.52, "end": 511.06, "text": " The actual song being played.", "tokens": [51465, 440, 3539, 2153, 885, 3737, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2164610716012808, "compression_ratio": 1.599236641221374, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806485011125696e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 51106, "start": 511.06, "end": 513.14, "text": " Exactly, the actual song.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 11, 264, 3539, 2153, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23416997540381648, "compression_ratio": 1.4021739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794580270414582e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 51106, "start": 513.74, "end": 521.32, "text": " But the tech platform's setup, as Fliction argues, frequently severs that connection completely, usually in the name of engagement.", "tokens": [50499, 583, 264, 7553, 3663, 311, 8657, 11, 382, 3235, 4105, 38218, 11, 10374, 369, 840, 300, 4984, 2584, 11, 2673, 294, 264, 1315, 295, 8742, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23416997540381648, "compression_ratio": 1.4021739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794580270414582e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 51106, "start": 521.62, "end": 521.86, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50893, 3153, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23416997540381648, "compression_ratio": 1.4021739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794580270414582e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 51106, "start": 522.0, "end": 522.22, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50912, 1033, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23416997540381648, "compression_ratio": 1.4021739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794580270414582e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 51106, "start": 522.34, "end": 526.42, "text": " We are going to dissect the mathematical difference between those two approaches shortly.", "tokens": [50929, 492, 366, 516, 281, 48332, 264, 18894, 2649, 1296, 729, 732, 11587, 13392, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23416997540381648, "compression_ratio": 1.4021739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794580270414582e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 52642, "start": 526.42, "end": 536.8399999999999, "text": " But that distinction between a healthy, coordinated projection and an isolated, severed reality, that is the beating heart of this text.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 300, 16844, 1296, 257, 4627, 11, 29591, 22743, 293, 364, 14621, 11, 2802, 292, 4103, 11, 300, 307, 264, 13497, 1917, 295, 341, 2487, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15427818081595682, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552082191505612e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 52642, "start": 537.0999999999999, "end": 537.4, "text": " I see.", "tokens": [50899, 286, 536, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15427818081595682, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552082191505612e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 52642, "start": 537.68, "end": 544.74, "text": " Well, before we can diagnose exactly where these massive digital systems go wrong, we have to look at the terminology we're using.", "tokens": [50928, 1042, 11, 949, 321, 393, 36238, 2293, 689, 613, 5994, 4562, 3652, 352, 2085, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 27575, 321, 434, 1228, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15427818081595682, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552082191505612e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 52642, "start": 544.88, "end": 545.1999999999999, "text": " Definitely.", "tokens": [51288, 12151, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15427818081595682, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552082191505612e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 52642, "start": 545.56, "end": 550.1999999999999, "text": " Because to understand what a monitor should be doing, we have to look at the word itself.", "tokens": [51322, 1436, 281, 1223, 437, 257, 6002, 820, 312, 884, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 1349, 2564, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15427818081595682, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552082191505612e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 55020, "start": 550.2, "end": 556.34, "text": " Fliction points out a linguistic accident surrounding the word monitor that is actually incredibly revealing.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 257, 43002, 6398, 11498, 264, 1349, 6002, 300, 307, 767, 6252, 23983, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 55020, "start": 556.6, "end": 559.5400000000001, "text": " It tells us so much about human psychology and system design.", "tokens": [50685, 467, 5112, 505, 370, 709, 466, 1952, 15105, 293, 1185, 1715, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 55020, "start": 559.6400000000001, "end": 559.7800000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50837, 865, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 55020, "start": 560.08, "end": 568.1, "text": " There are four distinct senses of the word monitor in English, and we use them all the time without realizing they describe very different relationships to reality.", "tokens": [50859, 821, 366, 1451, 10644, 17057, 295, 264, 1349, 6002, 294, 3669, 11, 293, 321, 764, 552, 439, 264, 565, 1553, 16734, 436, 6786, 588, 819, 6159, 281, 4103, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 55020, "start": 568.32, "end": 572.6800000000001, "text": " We use them interchangeably, but structurally, they dictate entirely different power dynamics.", "tokens": [51271, 492, 764, 552, 30358, 1188, 11, 457, 6594, 6512, 11, 436, 36071, 7696, 819, 1347, 15679, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 55020, "start": 572.7800000000001, "end": 574.08, "text": " Let's walk through the first three.", "tokens": [51494, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 264, 700, 1045, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13924436858206085, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553931398739397e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 57408, "start": 574.08, "end": 586.96, "text": " Sense number one, a monitor is an interface or a physical device that a person listens or watches through, like, I'm listening through my stage monitors, or I'm buying a new 4K monitor for my computer.", "tokens": [50365, 33123, 1230, 472, 11, 257, 6002, 307, 364, 9226, 420, 257, 4001, 4302, 300, 257, 954, 35959, 420, 17062, 807, 11, 411, 11, 286, 478, 4764, 807, 452, 3233, 26518, 11, 420, 286, 478, 6382, 257, 777, 1017, 42, 6002, 337, 452, 3820, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 57408, "start": 587.1800000000001, "end": 588.5600000000001, "text": " It is the physical window.", "tokens": [51020, 467, 307, 264, 4001, 4910, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 57408, "start": 588.76, "end": 589.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51099, 1779, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 57408, "start": 589.72, "end": 592.6600000000001, "text": " Sense number two, a monitor is a display of a state.", "tokens": [51147, 33123, 1230, 732, 11, 257, 6002, 307, 257, 4674, 295, 257, 1785, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 57408, "start": 593.0600000000001, "end": 596.76, "text": " It's a readout representing a system's condition at a given moment in time.", "tokens": [51314, 467, 311, 257, 1401, 346, 13460, 257, 1185, 311, 4188, 412, 257, 2212, 1623, 294, 565, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 57408, "start": 596.82, "end": 600.26, "text": " Like a heart rate monitor in a surgical theater displaying the beats per minute.", "tokens": [51502, 1743, 257, 1917, 3314, 6002, 294, 257, 26646, 10612, 36834, 264, 16447, 680, 3456, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 57408, "start": 600.5200000000001, "end": 601.24, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [51687, 10246, 1365, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 57408, "start": 601.24, "end": 603.44, "text": " And then sense number three is a bit more computational.", "tokens": [51723, 400, 550, 2020, 1230, 1045, 307, 257, 857, 544, 28270, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13231577614481135, "compression_ratio": 1.7653061224489797, "no_speech_prob": 1.9738212800324284e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 60344, "start": 603.44, "end": 603.9200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 60344, "start": 604.2600000000001, "end": 608.2800000000001, "text": " Sense three refers to a process that watches another process.", "tokens": [50406, 33123, 1045, 14942, 281, 257, 1399, 300, 17062, 1071, 1399, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 60344, "start": 608.5, "end": 608.5400000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50618, 1033, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 60344, "start": 609.0400000000001, "end": 612.2600000000001, "text": " It is an agent checking a system against an expectation.", "tokens": [50645, 467, 307, 364, 9461, 8568, 257, 1185, 1970, 364, 14334, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 60344, "start": 613.08, "end": 621.86, "text": " So in computer science, you have monitor programs or demons that run in the background supervising other software to ensure it doesn't leak memory or crash.", "tokens": [50847, 407, 294, 3820, 3497, 11, 291, 362, 6002, 4268, 420, 19733, 300, 1190, 294, 264, 3678, 37971, 3436, 661, 4722, 281, 5586, 309, 1177, 380, 17143, 4675, 420, 8252, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 60344, "start": 622.0400000000001, "end": 628.6400000000001, "text": " So you have the physical interface, the representation of the state, and the active process checking for errors or deviations.", "tokens": [51295, 407, 291, 362, 264, 4001, 9226, 11, 264, 10290, 295, 264, 1785, 11, 293, 264, 4967, 1399, 8568, 337, 13603, 420, 31219, 763, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394365797651575, "compression_ratio": 1.6733870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736786873610242e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 62864, "start": 628.64, "end": 631.4, "text": " Now, look back at the musician on the concert stage.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 574, 646, 412, 264, 19570, 322, 264, 8543, 3233, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19297466278076172, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 62864, "start": 631.86, "end": 637.4, "text": " Their in-ear monitor is performing all three of those functions simultaneously in perfect harmony.", "tokens": [50526, 6710, 294, 12, 14881, 6002, 307, 10205, 439, 1045, 295, 729, 6828, 16561, 294, 2176, 19410, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19297466278076172, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 62864, "start": 637.5, "end": 638.12, "text": " Oh, I see it.", "tokens": [50808, 876, 11, 286, 536, 309, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19297466278076172, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 62864, "start": 638.3199999999999, "end": 640.62, "text": " It is the physical device they listen through.", "tokens": [50849, 467, 307, 264, 4001, 4302, 436, 2140, 807, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19297466278076172, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 62864, "start": 640.96, "end": 645.36, "text": " It is displaying a highly curated version of the performance's current state.", "tokens": [50981, 467, 307, 36834, 257, 5405, 47851, 3037, 295, 264, 3389, 311, 2190, 1785, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19297466278076172, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 64536, "start": 645.36, "end": 650.92, "text": " And crucially, it allows the musician to perform that third function.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 309, 4045, 264, 19570, 281, 2042, 300, 2636, 2445, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 64536, "start": 651.3000000000001, "end": 651.98, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [50662, 3013, 307, 30, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 64536, "start": 652.08, "end": 655.02, "text": " They are checking their own playing against the rest of the band.", "tokens": [50701, 814, 366, 8568, 641, 1065, 2433, 1970, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 4116, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 64536, "start": 655.24, "end": 657.54, "text": " They are the process checking the process.", "tokens": [50859, 814, 366, 264, 1399, 8568, 264, 1399, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 64536, "start": 657.76, "end": 658.86, "text": " The tool empowers them.", "tokens": [50985, 440, 2290, 4012, 23054, 552, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 64536, "start": 658.96, "end": 659.3000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51045, 7587, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 64536, "start": 659.72, "end": 662.08, "text": " They are not merely being watched by the system.", "tokens": [51083, 814, 366, 406, 17003, 885, 6337, 538, 264, 1185, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 64536, "start": 662.26, "end": 665.88, "text": " They are actively wielding it to participate in a shared objective.", "tokens": [51210, 814, 366, 13022, 35982, 278, 309, 281, 8197, 294, 257, 5507, 10024, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18702360131274695, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686416788244673e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 66588, "start": 665.88, "end": 669.0, "text": " But then there is the dark fourth sense of the word.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 550, 456, 307, 264, 2877, 6409, 2020, 295, 264, 1349, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 66588, "start": 669.66, "end": 673.02, "text": " And honestly, this is the one most of us learn first as kids.", "tokens": [50554, 400, 6095, 11, 341, 307, 264, 472, 881, 295, 505, 1466, 700, 382, 2301, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 66588, "start": 673.26, "end": 674.96, "text": " The institutional use of the word.", "tokens": [50734, 440, 18391, 764, 295, 264, 1349, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 66588, "start": 675.2, "end": 675.6, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50831, 7587, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 66588, "start": 676.12, "end": 682.68, "text": " A monitor as a person posted to oversee a room, the middle school hall monitor, or an exam monitor.", "tokens": [50877, 316, 6002, 382, 257, 954, 9437, 281, 46543, 257, 1808, 11, 264, 2808, 1395, 6500, 6002, 11, 420, 364, 1139, 6002, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 66588, "start": 682.82, "end": 683.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51212, 1779, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 66588, "start": 683.24, "end": 685.02, "text": " Think about what that role actually is.", "tokens": [51233, 6557, 466, 437, 300, 3090, 767, 307, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 66588, "start": 685.4399999999999, "end": 687.3, "text": " They aren't there to help you learn the curriculum.", "tokens": [51343, 814, 3212, 380, 456, 281, 854, 291, 1466, 264, 14302, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 66588, "start": 687.68, "end": 690.26, "text": " They aren't facilitating your participation in the school's mission.", "tokens": [51455, 814, 3212, 380, 47558, 428, 13487, 294, 264, 1395, 311, 4447, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 66588, "start": 690.36, "end": 692.94, "text": " No, their sole function is surveillance and compliance.", "tokens": [51589, 883, 11, 641, 12321, 2445, 307, 18475, 293, 15882, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15960913557347242, "compression_ratio": 1.6971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942076659834157e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 69294, "start": 692.94, "end": 693.4200000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 69294, "start": 693.94, "end": 698.7, "text": " They are watching to ensure you don't run, don't cheat, don't deviate from the rules.", "tokens": [50415, 814, 366, 1976, 281, 5586, 291, 500, 380, 1190, 11, 500, 380, 17470, 11, 500, 380, 1905, 13024, 490, 264, 4474, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 69294, "start": 699.0600000000001, "end": 702.1400000000001, "text": " It is a purely supervisory, asymmetrical relationship.", "tokens": [50671, 467, 307, 257, 17491, 34409, 827, 11, 37277, 32283, 2480, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 69294, "start": 702.96, "end": 705.22, "text": " And Flixine's insight here is foundational.", "tokens": [50866, 400, 3235, 970, 533, 311, 11269, 510, 307, 32195, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 69294, "start": 705.8000000000001, "end": 708.3000000000001, "text": " When a system separates those first three functions,", "tokens": [51008, 1133, 257, 1185, 34149, 729, 700, 1045, 6828, 11, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 69294, "start": 708.9200000000001, "end": 717.1800000000001, "text": " when a tech platform or a corporate structure treats what a user sees as completely unrelated to what the system's actual state is,", "tokens": [51164, 562, 257, 7553, 3663, 420, 257, 10896, 3877, 19566, 437, 257, 4195, 8194, 382, 2584, 38967, 281, 437, 264, 1185, 311, 3539, 1785, 307, 11, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 69294, "start": 717.58, "end": 721.96, "text": " and separates that again from how the system checks for failure coordination degrades.", "tokens": [51597, 293, 34149, 300, 797, 490, 577, 264, 1185, 13834, 337, 7763, 21252, 368, 22626, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20087165832519532, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 2.020588991263894e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 72196, "start": 721.96, "end": 723.14, "text": " It breaks down.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 9857, 760, 13, 50424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 72196, "start": 723.48, "end": 723.72, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50441, 1079, 13, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 72196, "start": 723.98, "end": 729.6600000000001, "text": " When those functions are decoupled, the system devolves into that purely supervisory fourth sense.", "tokens": [50466, 1133, 729, 6828, 366, 979, 263, 15551, 11, 264, 1185, 1905, 401, 977, 666, 300, 17491, 34409, 827, 6409, 2020, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 72196, "start": 730.0, "end": 731.5600000000001, "text": " The platform is just watching the user.", "tokens": [50767, 440, 3663, 307, 445, 1976, 264, 4195, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 72196, "start": 731.84, "end": 732.64, "text": " Like it tracking clicks.", "tokens": [50859, 1743, 309, 11603, 18521, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 72196, "start": 733.0400000000001, "end": 733.52, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50919, 7587, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 72196, "start": 733.98, "end": 738.26, "text": " It's tracking your clicks, monitoring your engagement, checking you for gross policy violations,", "tokens": [50966, 467, 311, 11603, 428, 18521, 11, 11028, 428, 8742, 11, 8568, 291, 337, 11367, 3897, 30405, 11, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 72196, "start": 738.6600000000001, "end": 742.46, "text": " but it is not empowering you to understand the shared state of the network.", "tokens": [51200, 457, 309, 307, 406, 28261, 291, 281, 1223, 264, 5507, 1785, 295, 264, 3209, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 72196, "start": 742.6, "end": 743.62, "text": " It's just a hall monitor.", "tokens": [51397, 467, 311, 445, 257, 6500, 6002, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 72196, "start": 743.84, "end": 744.1600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51459, 1079, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 72196, "start": 744.7, "end": 748.88, "text": " Uniting those first three functions in a single tool is not a UX convenience.", "tokens": [51502, 1156, 1748, 729, 700, 1045, 6828, 294, 257, 2167, 2290, 307, 406, 257, 40176, 19283, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205432922859502, "compression_ratio": 1.6725352112676057, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047204797614567e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 74888, "start": 748.88, "end": 756.42, "text": " It is an absolute necessity for any system that wants healthy, autonomous coordination among its participants.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 364, 8236, 24217, 337, 604, 1185, 300, 2738, 4627, 11, 23797, 21252, 3654, 1080, 10503, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 74888, "start": 756.86, "end": 757.54, "text": " I love that framing.", "tokens": [50764, 286, 959, 300, 28971, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 74888, "start": 758.26, "end": 762.16, "text": " A healthy monitor expands an agent's capacity to perceive and act,", "tokens": [50834, 316, 4627, 6002, 33706, 364, 9461, 311, 6042, 281, 20281, 293, 605, 11, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 74888, "start": 762.36, "end": 766.7, "text": " while a degraded monitor just watches the agent to enforce compliance.", "tokens": [51039, 1339, 257, 24740, 292, 6002, 445, 17062, 264, 9461, 281, 24825, 15882, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 74888, "start": 767.16, "end": 767.4399999999999, "text": " All right.", "tokens": [51279, 1057, 558, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 74888, "start": 767.48, "end": 770.76, "text": " So we know what a healthy monitor should be doing conceptually.", "tokens": [51295, 407, 321, 458, 437, 257, 4627, 6002, 820, 312, 884, 3410, 671, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 74888, "start": 771.18, "end": 774.54, "text": " Let's look at the actual physics and mathematics of what it transmits to the user.", "tokens": [51480, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 3539, 10649, 293, 18666, 295, 437, 309, 7715, 1208, 281, 264, 4195, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 74888, "start": 774.82, "end": 776.22, "text": " How does it actually work?", "tokens": [51662, 1012, 775, 309, 767, 589, 30, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625485108277508, "compression_ratio": 1.6389891696750902, "no_speech_prob": 1.531097948079263e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 77622, "start": 776.22, "end": 781.32, "text": " This brings us to the core concept of the essay, the shared state.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 3410, 295, 264, 16238, 11, 264, 5507, 1785, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 77622, "start": 781.88, "end": 784.1800000000001, "text": " Fliction uses a very specific notation for this, right?", "tokens": [50648, 3235, 4105, 4960, 257, 588, 2685, 24657, 337, 341, 11, 558, 30, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 77622, "start": 784.26, "end": 784.4, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50767, 865, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 77622, "start": 784.6800000000001, "end": 789.34, "text": " The shared state is represented mathematically as a continuing event evolving in time.", "tokens": [50788, 440, 5507, 1785, 307, 10379, 44003, 382, 257, 9289, 2280, 21085, 294, 565, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 77622, "start": 789.5400000000001, "end": 789.86, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51031, 1079, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 77622, "start": 789.98, "end": 794.26, "text": " The essay uses the variable S moving through time T, so S of T.", "tokens": [51053, 440, 16238, 4960, 264, 7006, 318, 2684, 807, 565, 314, 11, 370, 318, 295, 314, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 77622, "start": 794.6800000000001, "end": 800.28, "text": " Now, we're not going to read out algebraic formulas on an audio show because that is a total nightmare to listen to.", "tokens": [51288, 823, 11, 321, 434, 406, 516, 281, 1401, 484, 21989, 299, 30546, 322, 364, 6278, 855, 570, 300, 307, 257, 3217, 18724, 281, 2140, 281, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 77622, "start": 800.5, "end": 800.74, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51579, 883, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12301646437600394, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401915723854e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 80074, "start": 800.74, "end": 803.72, "text": " But let's translate the math into spatial reality.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 718, 311, 13799, 264, 5221, 666, 23598, 4103, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723155975341797, "compression_ratio": 1.5446009389671362, "no_speech_prob": 1.361789045244144e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 80074, "start": 804.7, "end": 806.64, "text": " Imagine S is the entirety of the room.", "tokens": [50563, 11739, 318, 307, 264, 31557, 295, 264, 1808, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723155975341797, "compression_ratio": 1.5446009389671362, "no_speech_prob": 1.361789045244144e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 80074, "start": 807.16, "end": 815.74, "text": " On the concert stage, this is the pure, unmixed, raw sound of every single instrument, every voice, the crowd noise, the reflections off the back wall.", "tokens": [50686, 1282, 264, 8543, 3233, 11, 341, 307, 264, 6075, 11, 19334, 40303, 11, 8936, 1626, 295, 633, 2167, 7198, 11, 633, 3177, 11, 264, 6919, 5658, 11, 264, 30679, 766, 264, 646, 2929, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723155975341797, "compression_ratio": 1.5446009389671362, "no_speech_prob": 1.361789045244144e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 80074, "start": 815.9, "end": 821.36, "text": " The literal, objective, acoustic truth of the physical space in that exact millisecond.", "tokens": [51123, 440, 20411, 11, 10024, 11, 26753, 3494, 295, 264, 4001, 1901, 294, 300, 1900, 27940, 18882, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723155975341797, "compression_ratio": 1.5446009389671362, "no_speech_prob": 1.361789045244144e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 82136, "start": 821.36, "end": 824.12, "text": " But here is the massive twist that Fliction introduces.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 510, 307, 264, 5994, 8203, 300, 3235, 4105, 31472, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 82136, "start": 824.84, "end": 826.96, "text": " Nobody in the band experiences the room.", "tokens": [50539, 9297, 294, 264, 4116, 5235, 264, 1808, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 82136, "start": 827.08, "end": 827.88, "text": " Not a single person.", "tokens": [50651, 1726, 257, 2167, 954, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 82136, "start": 828.14, "end": 829.22, "text": " It's crazy to think about.", "tokens": [50704, 467, 311, 3219, 281, 519, 466, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 82136, "start": 829.32, "end": 835.42, "text": " The pure, unadulterated reality of the room is structurally inaccessible to the people actually creating it.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 6075, 11, 517, 345, 425, 391, 770, 4103, 295, 264, 1808, 307, 6594, 6512, 33230, 780, 964, 281, 264, 561, 767, 4084, 309, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 82136, "start": 835.62, "end": 837.02, "text": " Instead, they receive a projection.", "tokens": [51078, 7156, 11, 436, 4774, 257, 22743, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14688870813939478, "compression_ratio": 1.4820512820512821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074956257257743e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 83702, "start": 837.02, "end": 847.96, "text": " The system takes the totality of the room, applies a strict mathematical filter to it, and projects a highly specific slice of that reality directly into the ear of person A.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 2516, 264, 1993, 1860, 295, 264, 1808, 11, 13165, 257, 10910, 18894, 6608, 281, 309, 11, 293, 4455, 257, 5405, 2685, 13153, 295, 300, 4103, 3838, 666, 264, 1273, 295, 954, 316, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09491931824457078, "compression_ratio": 1.5694444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691697716190613e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 83702, "start": 848.06, "end": 848.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50917, 1079, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09491931824457078, "compression_ratio": 1.5694444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691697716190613e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 83702, "start": 848.52, "end": 852.98, "text": " And it throws away 90% of the room and only delivers the 10% that person A needs.", "tokens": [50940, 400, 309, 19251, 1314, 4289, 4, 295, 264, 1808, 293, 787, 24860, 264, 1266, 4, 300, 954, 316, 2203, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09491931824457078, "compression_ratio": 1.5694444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691697716190613e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 83702, "start": 853.12, "end": 855.96, "text": " And this is where we have to aggressively dismantle the sameness myth, right?", "tokens": [51170, 400, 341, 307, 689, 321, 362, 281, 32024, 30506, 306, 264, 3247, 15264, 9474, 11, 558, 30, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09491931824457078, "compression_ratio": 1.5694444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691697716190613e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 85596, "start": 855.96, "end": 857.98, "text": " Fliction is so adamant about this.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 307, 370, 16368, 394, 466, 341, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 85596, "start": 858.32, "end": 874.0400000000001, "text": " In social design, in political theory, in software architecture, we have this deep-seated, almost invisible assumption that for coordination to be fair or successful, participant A's reality must be perfectly identical to participant B's reality.", "tokens": [50483, 682, 2093, 1715, 11, 294, 3905, 5261, 11, 294, 4722, 9482, 11, 321, 362, 341, 2452, 12, 405, 770, 11, 1920, 14603, 15302, 300, 337, 21252, 281, 312, 3143, 420, 4406, 11, 24950, 316, 311, 4103, 1633, 312, 6239, 14800, 281, 24950, 363, 311, 4103, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 85596, "start": 874.22, "end": 876.1, "text": " We assume the projections must match.", "tokens": [51278, 492, 6552, 264, 32371, 1633, 2995, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 85596, "start": 876.34, "end": 878.6600000000001, "text": " Like, M sub I has to equal M sub J.", "tokens": [51384, 1743, 11, 376, 1422, 286, 575, 281, 2681, 376, 1422, 508, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 85596, "start": 878.76, "end": 879.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51505, 1079, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 85596, "start": 879.1600000000001, "end": 882.74, "text": " We treat identical information as the prerequisite for shared truth.", "tokens": [51525, 492, 2387, 14800, 1589, 382, 264, 38333, 34152, 337, 5507, 3494, 13, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11029244404213101, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.6944907933399977e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 88274, "start": 882.74, "end": 889.92, "text": " Infliction argues that treating identical projection as the goal of coordination technology is the fundamental failure of modern systems.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 3423, 4105, 38218, 300, 15083, 14800, 22743, 382, 264, 3387, 295, 21252, 2899, 307, 264, 8088, 7763, 295, 4363, 3652, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 88274, "start": 890.08, "end": 890.94, "text": " It was never the goal.", "tokens": [50732, 467, 390, 1128, 264, 3387, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 88274, "start": 891.0600000000001, "end": 891.26, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50781, 883, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 88274, "start": 891.7, "end": 901.94, "text": " The rock band is the ultimate proof that you can have flawlessly coordinated, highly complex, synchronous behavior between agents whose projections of reality share almost nothing in common.", "tokens": [50813, 440, 3727, 4116, 307, 264, 9705, 8177, 300, 291, 393, 362, 13717, 12048, 29591, 11, 5405, 3997, 11, 44743, 5223, 1296, 12554, 6104, 32371, 295, 4103, 2073, 1920, 1825, 294, 2689, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 88274, "start": 902.3, "end": 903.98, "text": " Let's ground this outside of music.", "tokens": [51343, 961, 311, 2727, 341, 2380, 295, 1318, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 88274, "start": 904.3, "end": 909.44, "text": " Because I was trying to think of an analogy for how this works in, like, daily human interaction.", "tokens": [51443, 1436, 286, 390, 1382, 281, 519, 295, 364, 21663, 337, 577, 341, 1985, 294, 11, 411, 11, 5212, 1952, 9285, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 88274, "start": 909.8, "end": 910.74, "text": " Oh, I'd love to hear it.", "tokens": [51718, 876, 11, 286, 1116, 959, 281, 1568, 309, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 88274, "start": 910.88, "end": 912.32, "text": " Think about a group of friends.", "tokens": [51772, 6557, 466, 257, 1594, 295, 1855, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11746339644155195, "compression_ratio": 1.649546827794562, "no_speech_prob": 1.965929155578472e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 91274, "start": 912.74, "end": 916.52, "text": " Who take a massive two-week cross-country road trip together.", "tokens": [50365, 2102, 747, 257, 5994, 732, 12, 23188, 3278, 12, 39337, 3060, 4931, 1214, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 91274, "start": 916.98, "end": 918.86, "text": " They are all in the same car.", "tokens": [50577, 814, 366, 439, 294, 264, 912, 1032, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 91274, "start": 919.4, "end": 923.5600000000001, "text": " They are sharing the exact same physical state moving through time.", "tokens": [50698, 814, 366, 5414, 264, 1900, 912, 4001, 1785, 2684, 807, 565, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 91274, "start": 924.08, "end": 924.38, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50932, 1033, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 91274, "start": 924.5600000000001, "end": 925.08, "text": " S of T.", "tokens": [50956, 318, 295, 314, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 91274, "start": 925.42, "end": 926.46, "text": " The car on the road.", "tokens": [50999, 440, 1032, 322, 264, 3060, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 91274, "start": 926.7, "end": 927.1800000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51063, 7587, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 91274, "start": 927.5, "end": 927.7, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51103, 865, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 91274, "start": 927.7, "end": 932.7, "text": " Now, imagine a month later, they are at a dinner party telling a story about that trip.", "tokens": [51113, 823, 11, 3811, 257, 1618, 1780, 11, 436, 366, 412, 257, 6148, 3595, 3585, 257, 1657, 466, 300, 4931, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 91274, "start": 933.08, "end": 940.96, "text": " If all four of them sat down and repeated the exact same sentences, word for word, describing the exact same details in the exact same order.", "tokens": [51382, 759, 439, 1451, 295, 552, 3227, 760, 293, 10477, 264, 1900, 912, 16579, 11, 1349, 337, 1349, 11, 16141, 264, 1900, 912, 4365, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 1668, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 91274, "start": 941.12, "end": 942.26, "text": " That would be terrifying.", "tokens": [51784, 663, 576, 312, 18106, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18343967199325562, "compression_ratio": 1.7158671586715868, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893067228216044e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 94226, "start": 942.26, "end": 942.78, "text": " It would.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 94226, "start": 942.96, "end": 944.84, "text": " It wouldn't feel like a shared human memory.", "tokens": [50400, 467, 2759, 380, 841, 411, 257, 5507, 1952, 4675, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 94226, "start": 945.1, "end": 947.1, "text": " It would feel incredibly, deeply unsettling.", "tokens": [50507, 467, 576, 841, 6252, 11, 8760, 43964, 1688, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 94226, "start": 947.18, "end": 949.16, "text": " They would sound like programmed robots.", "tokens": [50611, 814, 576, 1626, 411, 31092, 14733, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 94226, "start": 949.38, "end": 949.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50721, 1779, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 94226, "start": 949.98, "end": 956.4399999999999, "text": " The richness and the truth of the shared experience actually comes from the fact that their memories, their projections are totally different.", "tokens": [50751, 440, 44506, 293, 264, 3494, 295, 264, 5507, 1752, 767, 1487, 490, 264, 1186, 300, 641, 8495, 11, 641, 32371, 366, 3879, 819, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 94226, "start": 956.58, "end": 957.38, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51081, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1314049018056769, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741041945443787e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 95738, "start": 957.38, "end": 962.08, "text": " The person who drove remembers the physical stress of the mountain passes and the sound of the engine.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 954, 567, 13226, 26228, 264, 4001, 4244, 295, 264, 6937, 11335, 293, 264, 1626, 295, 264, 2848, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704289118448892, "compression_ratio": 1.7150837988826815, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482866283141663e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 95738, "start": 962.22, "end": 967.66, "text": " The passenger remembers the intricate details of the playlists they were curating and the weird billboards.", "tokens": [50607, 440, 18707, 26228, 264, 38015, 4365, 295, 264, 862, 36693, 436, 645, 1262, 990, 293, 264, 3657, 2961, 17228, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704289118448892, "compression_ratio": 1.7150837988826815, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482866283141663e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 95738, "start": 968.3, "end": 972.66, "text": " And the person in the back seat just remembers the angle of the sun and sleeping through Nevada.", "tokens": [50911, 400, 264, 954, 294, 264, 646, 6121, 445, 26228, 264, 5802, 295, 264, 3295, 293, 8296, 807, 25764, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704289118448892, "compression_ratio": 1.7150837988826815, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482866283141663e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 97266, "start": 972.66, "end": 973.1, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19730270610136144, "compression_ratio": 1.3245614035087718, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426270066371984e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 97266, "start": 973.1, "end": 982.5, "text": " Their individual projections are wildly distinct, but they all effortlessly map back to the exact same vehicle moving down the exact same highway.", "tokens": [50387, 6710, 2609, 32371, 366, 34731, 10644, 11, 457, 436, 439, 4630, 12048, 4471, 646, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 5864, 2684, 760, 264, 1900, 912, 17205, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19730270610136144, "compression_ratio": 1.3245614035087718, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426270066371984e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 98250, "start": 982.5, "end": 984.92, "text": " That is a phenomenal analogy.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 17778, 21663, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21451148620018592, "compression_ratio": 1.5338345864661653, "no_speech_prob": 1.68815796845051e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 98250, "start": 985.34, "end": 990.64, "text": " Because what makes that storytelling at the dinner party work isn't that their mental contents are identical.", "tokens": [50507, 1436, 437, 1669, 300, 21479, 412, 264, 6148, 3595, 589, 1943, 380, 300, 641, 4973, 15768, 366, 14800, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21451148620018592, "compression_ratio": 1.5338345864661653, "no_speech_prob": 1.68815796845051e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 98250, "start": 990.96, "end": 993.42, "text": " It's that their mental contents are compatible.", "tokens": [50788, 467, 311, 300, 641, 4973, 15768, 366, 18218, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21451148620018592, "compression_ratio": 1.5338345864661653, "no_speech_prob": 1.68815796845051e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 98250, "start": 993.86, "end": 994.42, "text": " Compatible.", "tokens": [50933, 6620, 267, 964, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21451148620018592, "compression_ratio": 1.5338345864661653, "no_speech_prob": 1.68815796845051e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 98250, "start": 994.62, "end": 994.92, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50971, 1079, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21451148620018592, "compression_ratio": 1.5338345864661653, "no_speech_prob": 1.68815796845051e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 99492, "start": 994.92, "end": 999.92, "text": " This is Flickshane's true requirement for coordination, the compatibility condition.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 3235, 618, 2716, 1929, 311, 2074, 11695, 337, 21252, 11, 264, 34237, 4188, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 99492, "start": 1000.68, "end": 1001.8199999999999, "text": " So it's not about sameness.", "tokens": [50653, 407, 309, 311, 406, 466, 3247, 15264, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 99492, "start": 1002.18, "end": 1004.0, "text": " It is exclusively about compatibility.", "tokens": [50728, 467, 307, 20638, 466, 34237, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 99492, "start": 1004.24, "end": 1004.8, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50831, 48746, 736, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 99492, "start": 1004.8, "end": 1015.8199999999999, "text": " The whole set of projections, everyone's individual memory of the road trip or every musician's individual monitor mix, must function as a working set of views onto the same underlying event.", "tokens": [50859, 440, 1379, 992, 295, 32371, 11, 1518, 311, 2609, 4675, 295, 264, 3060, 4931, 420, 633, 19570, 311, 2609, 6002, 2890, 11, 1633, 2445, 382, 257, 1364, 992, 295, 6809, 3911, 264, 912, 14217, 2280, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 99492, "start": 1016.0, "end": 1016.0999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51419, 1779, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 99492, "start": 1016.4799999999999, "end": 1024.1399999999999, "text": " The drummer's mix and the singer's mix are radically different, but they are both faithful, usable guides back to the architecture of the song.", "tokens": [51443, 440, 38535, 311, 2890, 293, 264, 11564, 311, 2890, 366, 35508, 819, 11, 457, 436, 366, 1293, 17808, 11, 29975, 17007, 646, 281, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 2153, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1364863083280366, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256839604494315e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 102414, "start": 1024.14, "end": 1028.98, "text": " And, you know, when we were prepping for this, I noticed you got completely sidetracked by the footnotes in this section.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 11, 291, 458, 11, 562, 321, 645, 659, 3759, 337, 341, 11, 286, 5694, 291, 658, 2584, 20822, 27965, 25949, 538, 264, 2671, 2247, 279, 294, 341, 3541, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 102414, "start": 1029.0600000000002, "end": 1030.3000000000002, "text": " Oh my gosh, I fully admit it.", "tokens": [50611, 876, 452, 6502, 11, 286, 4498, 9796, 309, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 102414, "start": 1030.5, "end": 1035.26, "text": " You were practically vibrating with excitement over the psychological theory backing this up.", "tokens": [50683, 509, 645, 15667, 47748, 365, 14755, 670, 264, 14346, 5261, 19373, 341, 493, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 102414, "start": 1035.5200000000002, "end": 1040.5, "text": " I really went down a massive rabbit hole here because Flickshane isn't just making this up.", "tokens": [50934, 286, 534, 1437, 760, 257, 5994, 19509, 5458, 510, 570, 3235, 618, 2716, 1929, 1943, 380, 445, 1455, 341, 493, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 102414, "start": 1041.0, "end": 1045.94, "text": " Footnote 1 connects this compatibility condition directly to foundational cognitive psychology.", "tokens": [51208, 20989, 22178, 502, 16967, 341, 34237, 4188, 3838, 281, 32195, 15605, 15105, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 102414, "start": 1046.1200000000001, "end": 1046.8200000000002, "text": " Who are the researchers?", "tokens": [51464, 2102, 366, 264, 10309, 30, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 102414, "start": 1047.26, "end": 1052.64, "text": " It references Herbert Clark and Susan Brennan's 1991 conversational grounding theory.", "tokens": [51521, 467, 15400, 41942, 18572, 293, 15160, 31200, 17622, 311, 24097, 2615, 1478, 46727, 5261, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12899204967467764, "compression_ratio": 1.6142433234421365, "no_speech_prob": 1.935457653520767e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 105264, "start": 1052.64, "end": 1054.2800000000002, "text": " Okay, what does that say?", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 437, 775, 300, 584, 30, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 105264, "start": 1054.72, "end": 1063.66, "text": " Well, Clark and Brennan established that successful human communication does not mean two people have identical mental contents.", "tokens": [50469, 1042, 11, 18572, 293, 31200, 17622, 7545, 300, 4406, 1952, 6101, 775, 406, 914, 732, 561, 362, 14800, 4973, 15768, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 105264, "start": 1063.94, "end": 1068.0400000000002, "text": " It doesn't mean I copy a file from my brain and paste it into yours.", "tokens": [50930, 467, 1177, 380, 914, 286, 5055, 257, 3991, 490, 452, 3567, 293, 9163, 309, 666, 6342, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 105264, "start": 1068.14, "end": 1068.8400000000001, "text": " Thank goodness.", "tokens": [51140, 1044, 8387, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 105264, "start": 1069.0400000000002, "end": 1069.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51185, 1779, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 105264, "start": 1069.5600000000002, "end": 1074.18, "text": " Communication rests on a mutually maintained common ground that gets updated turn by turn.", "tokens": [51211, 34930, 39755, 322, 257, 39144, 17578, 2689, 2727, 300, 2170, 10588, 1261, 538, 1261, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 105264, "start": 1074.6000000000001, "end": 1075.38, "text": " I say a sentence.", "tokens": [51463, 286, 584, 257, 8174, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 105264, "start": 1075.9, "end": 1079.72, "text": " You process it through your unique context, adjust your internal model, and reply.", "tokens": [51528, 509, 1399, 309, 807, 428, 3845, 4319, 11, 4369, 428, 6920, 2316, 11, 293, 16972, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17439761528602013, "compression_ratio": 1.5812274368231047, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482959524528496e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 107972, "start": 1079.72, "end": 1086.26, "text": " I hear your reply, realize you maybe slightly misunderstood my tone, and I adjust my next sentence to correct it.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 1568, 428, 16972, 11, 4325, 291, 1310, 4748, 33870, 452, 8027, 11, 293, 286, 4369, 452, 958, 8174, 281, 3006, 309, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 107972, "start": 1086.52, "end": 1088.52, "text": " It's a continuous dynamic coupling.", "tokens": [50705, 467, 311, 257, 10957, 8546, 37447, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 107972, "start": 1088.84, "end": 1092.78, "text": " It is a shared activity of navigation, not a static copying of data.", "tokens": [50821, 467, 307, 257, 5507, 5191, 295, 17346, 11, 406, 257, 13437, 27976, 295, 1412, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 107972, "start": 1092.8600000000001, "end": 1094.5, "text": " Which maps perfectly back onto the stage.", "tokens": [51022, 3013, 11317, 6239, 646, 3911, 264, 3233, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 107972, "start": 1094.82, "end": 1098.1000000000001, "text": " Like, the drummer plays a slightly aggressive fill heading into the chorus.", "tokens": [51120, 1743, 11, 264, 38535, 5749, 257, 4748, 10762, 2836, 9864, 666, 264, 22632, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 107972, "start": 1098.2, "end": 1098.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51289, 1079, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 107972, "start": 1098.68, "end": 1104.04, "text": " The guitarist hears that dynamic shift in their monitor and instinctively digs into their strings a bit harder.", "tokens": [51313, 440, 7531, 468, 25688, 300, 8546, 5513, 294, 641, 6002, 293, 16556, 3413, 2528, 82, 666, 641, 13985, 257, 857, 6081, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314388239495108, "compression_ratio": 1.612099644128114, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546379288078338e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 110404, "start": 1104.04, "end": 1109.22, "text": " The singer feels the energy rise behind them and pushes the vocal higher.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 11564, 3417, 264, 2281, 6272, 2261, 552, 293, 21020, 264, 11657, 2946, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 110404, "start": 1109.56, "end": 1115.04, "text": " They are updating their shared reality turn by turn based on compatible but distinct inputs.", "tokens": [50641, 814, 366, 25113, 641, 5507, 4103, 1261, 538, 1261, 2361, 322, 18218, 457, 10644, 15743, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 110404, "start": 1115.84, "end": 1117.08, "text": " And there was another footnote, right?", "tokens": [50955, 400, 456, 390, 1071, 2671, 22178, 11, 558, 30, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 110404, "start": 1117.6, "end": 1118.42, "text": " About the math.", "tokens": [51043, 7769, 264, 5221, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 110404, "start": 1118.54, "end": 1118.82, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51090, 1079, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 110404, "start": 1119.06, "end": 1122.32, "text": " Footnote 2 gets into the mathematical nuance of how we measure this.", "tokens": [51116, 20989, 22178, 568, 2170, 666, 264, 18894, 42625, 295, 577, 321, 3481, 341, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 110404, "start": 1122.96, "end": 1128.3799999999999, "text": " Fushin notes that this compatibility condition isn't just a simple threshold number you can measure on a spreadsheet.", "tokens": [51311, 479, 1498, 259, 5570, 300, 341, 34237, 4188, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 2199, 14678, 1230, 291, 393, 3481, 322, 257, 27733, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 110404, "start": 1128.68, "end": 1129.34, "text": " What is it then?", "tokens": [51597, 708, 307, 309, 550, 30, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16949793008657602, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039738098109883e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 112934, "start": 1129.34, "end": 1131.4599999999998, "text": " It's a topological condition.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 1192, 4383, 4188, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 112934, "start": 1132.06, "end": 1137.1399999999999, "text": " Think of it as phase locking, or path consistency across overlapping local views.", "tokens": [50501, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 5574, 23954, 11, 420, 3100, 14416, 2108, 33535, 2654, 6809, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 112934, "start": 1137.22, "end": 1138.3999999999999, "text": " Okay, I have to stop you there.", "tokens": [50759, 1033, 11, 286, 362, 281, 1590, 291, 456, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 112934, "start": 1139.1399999999999, "end": 1144.3999999999999, "text": " Topological phase locking is a terrifying phrase for anyone who hasn't taken advanced physics.", "tokens": [50855, 8840, 4383, 5574, 23954, 307, 257, 18106, 9535, 337, 2878, 567, 6132, 380, 2726, 7339, 10649, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 112934, "start": 1144.6599999999999, "end": 1145.54, "text": " Huh. Fair enough.", "tokens": [51131, 8063, 13, 12157, 1547, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 112934, "start": 1145.8, "end": 1149.48, "text": " Let's break down the mechanism of what that actually means in the physical world.", "tokens": [51188, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 7513, 295, 437, 300, 767, 1355, 294, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 112934, "start": 1149.6399999999999, "end": 1149.86, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51380, 876, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 112934, "start": 1150.08, "end": 1155.02, "text": " Phase locking just means that two independent oscillating systems align their rhythms, right?", "tokens": [51402, 24432, 23954, 445, 1355, 300, 732, 6695, 18225, 990, 3652, 7975, 641, 44892, 11, 558, 30, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 112934, "start": 1155.02, "end": 1155.76, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [51649, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645621394251918, "compression_ratio": 1.5957446808510638, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622700174135808e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 115576, "start": 1155.76, "end": 1160.94, "text": " Like two pendulum clocks on the same wall eventually swinging in unison because of the micro vibrations in the wood.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 732, 44103, 41528, 322, 264, 912, 2929, 4728, 29500, 294, 517, 2770, 570, 295, 264, 4532, 32339, 294, 264, 4576, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 115576, "start": 1161.02, "end": 1161.8799999999999, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [50628, 10246, 1365, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 115576, "start": 1162.36, "end": 1168.74, "text": " So on stage, the drummer has an internal metronome, and the bassist has an internal metronome.", "tokens": [50695, 407, 322, 3233, 11, 264, 38535, 575, 364, 6920, 1131, 2044, 423, 11, 293, 264, 10136, 468, 575, 364, 6920, 1131, 2044, 423, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 115576, "start": 1169.08, "end": 1170.24, "text": " They're independent systems.", "tokens": [51031, 814, 434, 6695, 3652, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 115576, "start": 1170.72, "end": 1176.0, "text": " But the sound waves of the bass hit the drummer's ear, and the sound waves of the kick drum hit the bassist's ear.", "tokens": [51113, 583, 264, 1626, 9417, 295, 264, 10136, 2045, 264, 38535, 311, 1273, 11, 293, 264, 1626, 9417, 295, 264, 4437, 10206, 2045, 264, 10136, 468, 311, 1273, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 115576, "start": 1176.12, "end": 1176.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51383, 1779, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 115576, "start": 1176.82, "end": 1182.84, "text": " Those distinct views force their internal metronomes to align to lock into the same phase in time.", "tokens": [51418, 3950, 10644, 6809, 3464, 641, 6920, 1131, 2044, 18168, 281, 7975, 281, 4017, 666, 264, 912, 5574, 294, 565, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391744613647461, "compression_ratio": 1.8314176245210727, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736443382378788e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 118284, "start": 1182.84, "end": 1185.1999999999998, "text": " They don't need to share the same melodic information.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 500, 380, 643, 281, 2073, 264, 912, 32834, 299, 1589, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 118284, "start": 1185.58, "end": 1189.56, "text": " They just need their temporal realities to lock together so the song doesn't collapse.", "tokens": [50502, 814, 445, 643, 641, 30881, 27785, 281, 4017, 1214, 370, 264, 2153, 1177, 380, 15584, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 118284, "start": 1189.9399999999998, "end": 1190.8999999999999, "text": " That is exactly right.", "tokens": [50720, 663, 307, 2293, 558, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 118284, "start": 1191.1999999999998, "end": 1198.52, "text": " They are tethered to the same underlying event through their overlapping edges, even if the center of their interfaces are totally distinct.", "tokens": [50783, 814, 366, 256, 1666, 292, 281, 264, 912, 14217, 2280, 807, 641, 33535, 8819, 11, 754, 498, 264, 3056, 295, 641, 28416, 366, 3879, 10644, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 118284, "start": 1198.9399999999998, "end": 1199.24, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51170, 3153, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 118284, "start": 1199.6399999999999, "end": 1201.82, "text": " Okay, so this brings us to the terrifying part of the essay.", "tokens": [51205, 1033, 11, 370, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 18106, 644, 295, 264, 16238, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 118284, "start": 1202.02, "end": 1202.86, "text": " Ah, yes.", "tokens": [51324, 2438, 11, 2086, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 118284, "start": 1203.1399999999999, "end": 1204.02, "text": " The failure state.", "tokens": [51380, 440, 7763, 1785, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 118284, "start": 1204.12, "end": 1204.3999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51429, 1779, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15328716096423922, "compression_ratio": 1.6707818930041152, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970235759515174e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 120440, "start": 1204.4, "end": 1210.88, "text": " If compatibility is the goal, what happens when a system loses its grip on that underlying shared state?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 34237, 307, 264, 3387, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 1185, 18293, 1080, 12007, 322, 300, 14217, 5507, 1785, 30, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 120440, "start": 1211.0, "end": 1212.3000000000002, "text": " What happens when the tether snaps?", "tokens": [50695, 708, 2314, 562, 264, 256, 1666, 19206, 30, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 120440, "start": 1212.6200000000001, "end": 1213.1200000000001, "text": " Gets bad.", "tokens": [50776, 460, 1385, 1578, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 120440, "start": 1213.2800000000002, "end": 1215.3000000000002, "text": " This is the core thesis of the entire piece.", "tokens": [50809, 639, 307, 264, 4965, 22288, 295, 264, 2302, 2522, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 120440, "start": 1216.02, "end": 1219.2800000000002, "text": " The structural difference between a hall of monitors and a hall of mirrors.", "tokens": [50946, 440, 15067, 2649, 1296, 257, 6500, 295, 26518, 293, 257, 6500, 295, 24238, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 120440, "start": 1219.46, "end": 1221.68, "text": " This is the most crucial distinction Flixson makes.", "tokens": [51118, 639, 307, 264, 881, 11462, 16844, 3235, 970, 3015, 1669, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 120440, "start": 1222.26, "end": 1225.64, "text": " In a true hall of monitors, you have a property called recoverability.", "tokens": [51258, 682, 257, 2074, 6500, 295, 26518, 11, 291, 362, 257, 4707, 1219, 8114, 2310, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14661764612003247, "compression_ratio": 1.6909871244635193, "no_speech_prob": 2.3612342549966803e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 122564, "start": 1225.64, "end": 1234.8200000000002, "text": " Meaning that a participant, armed only with their weird, highly personalized, filtered mix, can still find their way back to the truth of the room.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 300, 257, 24950, 11, 16297, 787, 365, 641, 3657, 11, 5405, 28415, 11, 37111, 2890, 11, 393, 920, 915, 641, 636, 646, 281, 264, 3494, 295, 264, 1808, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 122564, "start": 1235.0800000000002, "end": 1235.3400000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50837, 1079, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 122564, "start": 1235.3600000000001, "end": 1240.96, "text": " They can take their in-ear monitor out, listen to the ambient noise of the stage, point to the sound engineer and say,", "tokens": [50851, 814, 393, 747, 641, 294, 12, 14881, 6002, 484, 11, 2140, 281, 264, 22997, 5658, 295, 264, 3233, 11, 935, 281, 264, 1626, 11403, 293, 584, 11, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 122564, "start": 1241.16, "end": 1243.94, "text": " Hey, the bass is rushing the tempo, give me more snare drum.", "tokens": [51141, 1911, 11, 264, 10136, 307, 25876, 264, 8972, 11, 976, 385, 544, 45018, 10206, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 122564, "start": 1244.2, "end": 1244.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51293, 1779, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 122564, "start": 1244.6000000000001, "end": 1252.3400000000001, "text": " They fundamentally know that they are experiencing a partial view of reality, and they have a mechanism to verify it against the whole.", "tokens": [51313, 814, 17879, 458, 300, 436, 366, 11139, 257, 14641, 1910, 295, 4103, 11, 293, 436, 362, 257, 7513, 281, 16888, 309, 1970, 264, 1379, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 122564, "start": 1252.5, "end": 1254.76, "text": " The path back to the shared state is recoverable.", "tokens": [51708, 440, 3100, 646, 281, 264, 5507, 1785, 307, 8114, 712, 13, 51821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195283591747284, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111059527092799e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 125476, "start": 1254.76, "end": 1255.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 125476, "start": 1255.92, "end": 1259.7, "text": " And there's a beautiful paradox embedded in this recoverability.", "tokens": [50423, 400, 456, 311, 257, 2238, 26221, 16741, 294, 341, 8114, 2310, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 125476, "start": 1260.84, "end": 1262.56, "text": " Discarding information is not a flaw.", "tokens": [50669, 19839, 515, 278, 1589, 307, 406, 257, 13717, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 125476, "start": 1262.82, "end": 1263.02, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [50768, 4083, 30, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 125476, "start": 1263.3, "end": 1266.18, "text": " Discarding information is the entire point of the system.", "tokens": [50792, 19839, 515, 278, 1589, 307, 264, 2302, 935, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 125476, "start": 1266.8799999999999, "end": 1270.42, "text": " A good monitor is what mathematicians call a lossy projection.", "tokens": [50971, 316, 665, 6002, 307, 437, 32811, 2567, 818, 257, 4470, 88, 22743, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 125476, "start": 1271.04, "end": 1275.72, "text": " It deliberately collapses a relevant distinction so the participant isn't overwhelmed.", "tokens": [51179, 467, 23506, 48765, 257, 7340, 16844, 370, 264, 24950, 1943, 380, 19042, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 125476, "start": 1276.04, "end": 1277.5, "text": " Oh, like equivalence relations.", "tokens": [51429, 876, 11, 411, 9052, 655, 2299, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 125476, "start": 1277.78, "end": 1278.06, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51516, 1079, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 125476, "start": 1278.42, "end": 1281.2, "text": " Flixson uses the concept of equivalence relations here.", "tokens": [51548, 3235, 970, 3015, 4960, 264, 3410, 295, 9052, 655, 2299, 510, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19997258456248157, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.4554195522376023e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 128120, "start": 1281.2, "end": 1290.7, "text": " For the drummer, the exact tone of the rhythm guitar, whether the guitarist is using a fuzz pedal or a clean tone, does not matter for the purpose of keeping time.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 264, 38535, 11, 264, 1900, 8027, 295, 264, 11801, 7531, 11, 1968, 264, 7531, 468, 307, 1228, 257, 283, 16740, 19122, 420, 257, 2541, 8027, 11, 775, 406, 1871, 337, 264, 4334, 295, 5145, 565, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 128120, "start": 1290.8, "end": 1291.8, "text": " It's irrelevant data.", "tokens": [50845, 467, 311, 28682, 1412, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 128120, "start": 1292.04, "end": 1294.1200000000001, "text": " So the monitor throws that data away.", "tokens": [50907, 407, 264, 6002, 19251, 300, 1412, 1314, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 128120, "start": 1294.4, "end": 1297.74, "text": " It treats a fuzzy guitar and a clean guitar as equivalent states.", "tokens": [51025, 467, 19566, 257, 34710, 7531, 293, 257, 2541, 7531, 382, 10344, 4368, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 128120, "start": 1298.32, "end": 1298.94, "text": " This is good.", "tokens": [51221, 639, 307, 665, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 128120, "start": 1299.26, "end": 1301.88, "text": " It reduces the drummer's cognitive load.", "tokens": [51268, 467, 18081, 264, 38535, 311, 15605, 3677, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11705930045481479, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234847667606633e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 130188, "start": 1301.88, "end": 1307.5400000000002, "text": " But wait, if throwing away data is good, how does this beautiful functional system fail?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 498, 10238, 1314, 1412, 307, 665, 11, 577, 775, 341, 2238, 11745, 1185, 3061, 30, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744256223951066, "compression_ratio": 1.4352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 2.3428368620126427e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 130188, "start": 1308.16, "end": 1309.7, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [50679, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744256223951066, "compression_ratio": 1.4352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 2.3428368620126427e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 130188, "start": 1309.9, "end": 1315.24, "text": " It fails through a concept borrowed directly from signal processing and digital imaging called aliasing.", "tokens": [50766, 467, 18199, 807, 257, 3410, 26805, 3838, 490, 6358, 9007, 293, 4562, 25036, 1219, 10198, 3349, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744256223951066, "compression_ratio": 1.4352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 2.3428368620126427e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 130188, "start": 1315.48, "end": 1315.92, "text": " Aliasing?", "tokens": [51045, 12020, 3349, 30, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744256223951066, "compression_ratio": 1.4352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 2.3428368620126427e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 131592, "start": 1315.92, "end": 1316.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 131592, "start": 1316.8600000000001, "end": 1325.18, "text": " A functional monitor discards irrelevant information, but it fails structurally when it discards crucial distinctions, creating a false equivalence.", "tokens": [50412, 316, 11745, 6002, 2983, 2287, 28682, 1589, 11, 457, 309, 18199, 6594, 6512, 562, 309, 2983, 2287, 11462, 1483, 49798, 11, 4084, 257, 7908, 9052, 655, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 131592, "start": 1325.72, "end": 1327.16, "text": " What do you mean by false equivalence?", "tokens": [50855, 708, 360, 291, 914, 538, 7908, 9052, 655, 30, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 131592, "start": 1327.38, "end": 1336.52, "text": " It's when two underlying states in the real world that actually require totally different responses from the user are flattened by the system and made to look identical.", "tokens": [50938, 467, 311, 562, 732, 14217, 4368, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 300, 767, 3651, 3879, 819, 13019, 490, 264, 4195, 366, 24183, 292, 538, 264, 1185, 293, 1027, 281, 574, 14800, 13, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 131592, "start": 1336.8000000000002, "end": 1339.0, "text": " I need an example of that because that sounds a bit abstract.", "tokens": [51409, 286, 643, 364, 1365, 295, 300, 570, 300, 3263, 257, 857, 12649, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 131592, "start": 1339.5800000000002, "end": 1342.6000000000001, "text": " Walk me through how aliasing actually tricks a user.", "tokens": [51548, 10818, 385, 807, 577, 10198, 3349, 767, 11733, 257, 4195, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11191558837890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3194092086249443e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 134260, "start": 1342.6, "end": 1346.5, "text": " Okay, let's use digital photography first, as it's the most common example of aliasing.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 764, 4562, 13865, 700, 11, 382, 309, 311, 264, 881, 2689, 1365, 295, 10198, 3349, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 134260, "start": 1347.1799999999998, "end": 1358.02, "text": " Have you ever taken a picture of someone wearing a finely striped shirt, and in the digital photo, the shirt suddenly has these weird, swirling, wavy patterns all over it that aren't there in real life?", "tokens": [50594, 3560, 291, 1562, 2726, 257, 3036, 295, 1580, 4769, 257, 31529, 3575, 3452, 8336, 11, 293, 294, 264, 4562, 5052, 11, 264, 8336, 5800, 575, 613, 3657, 11, 30310, 278, 11, 261, 15498, 8294, 439, 670, 309, 300, 3212, 380, 456, 294, 957, 993, 30, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 134260, "start": 1358.26, "end": 1359.9199999999998, "text": " Oh yeah, the war\u00e9 effect.", "tokens": [51148, 876, 1338, 11, 264, 1516, 526, 1802, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 134260, "start": 1360.12, "end": 1361.5, "text": " It completely ruins the photo.", "tokens": [51241, 467, 2584, 24747, 264, 5052, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 134260, "start": 1361.6, "end": 1362.8799999999999, "text": " Exactly, the war\u00e9 effect.", "tokens": [51315, 7587, 11, 264, 1516, 526, 1802, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 134260, "start": 1363.54, "end": 1366.76, "text": " The digital camera sensor has a specific grid of pixels.", "tokens": [51412, 440, 4562, 2799, 10200, 575, 257, 2685, 10748, 295, 18668, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 134260, "start": 1367.34, "end": 1369.9199999999998, "text": " The physical shirt has a very tight grid of stripes.", "tokens": [51602, 440, 4001, 8336, 575, 257, 588, 4524, 10748, 295, 27308, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 134260, "start": 1370.1999999999998, "end": 1370.4199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51745, 1779, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534768044948578, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393468172173133e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 137042, "start": 1370.42, "end": 1377.98, "text": " When the frequency of the stripes exceeds the resolution of the camera sensor, the camera can't accurately record the data, so it basically guesses.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 264, 7893, 295, 264, 27308, 43305, 264, 8669, 295, 264, 2799, 10200, 11, 264, 2799, 393, 380, 20095, 2136, 264, 1412, 11, 370, 309, 1936, 42703, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 137042, "start": 1378.44, "end": 1378.72, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50766, 2438, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 137042, "start": 1378.92, "end": 1383.8200000000002, "text": " It aliases the high-frequency stripes down into a low-frequency, wavy pattern.", "tokens": [50790, 467, 10198, 1957, 264, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 27308, 760, 666, 257, 2295, 12, 19325, 48154, 11, 261, 15498, 5102, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 137042, "start": 1384.1000000000001, "end": 1385.72, "text": " It creates a false reality.", "tokens": [51049, 467, 7829, 257, 7908, 4103, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 137042, "start": 1386.0800000000002, "end": 1387.68, "text": " Wow, okay, now apply that to the band.", "tokens": [51148, 3153, 11, 1392, 11, 586, 3079, 300, 281, 264, 4116, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 137042, "start": 1388.18, "end": 1393.74, "text": " Imagine the band suddenly speeds up the tempo by 10 beats per minute because the crowd is going wild.", "tokens": [51253, 11739, 264, 4116, 5800, 16411, 493, 264, 8972, 538, 1266, 16447, 680, 3456, 570, 264, 6919, 307, 516, 4868, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 137042, "start": 1394.26, "end": 1396.92, "text": " This change requires the drummer to play faster.", "tokens": [51557, 639, 1319, 7029, 264, 38535, 281, 862, 4663, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 137042, "start": 1397.14, "end": 1397.6200000000001, "text": " Obviously.", "tokens": [51701, 7580, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12524095355954945, "compression_ratio": 1.6546762589928057, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327292607516084e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 139762, "start": 1397.62, "end": 1405.6, "text": " But imagine the drummer's monitor mix is being run through a faulty algorithm that heavily compresses and time-stretches the audio to keep everything sounding uniform.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3811, 264, 38535, 311, 6002, 2890, 307, 885, 1190, 807, 257, 2050, 5773, 9284, 300, 10950, 14778, 279, 293, 565, 12, 372, 1505, 3781, 264, 6278, 281, 1066, 1203, 24931, 9452, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14622793197631836, "compression_ratio": 1.5350877192982457, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796981778226638e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 139762, "start": 1405.84, "end": 1406.3, "text": " Oh no.", "tokens": [50776, 876, 572, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14622793197631836, "compression_ratio": 1.5350877192982457, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796981778226638e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 139762, "start": 1406.9599999999998, "end": 1408.5, "text": " The underlying state changed.", "tokens": [50832, 440, 14217, 1785, 3105, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14622793197631836, "compression_ratio": 1.5350877192982457, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796981778226638e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 139762, "start": 1408.9199999999998, "end": 1413.0, "text": " It demands a physical response, but the projection collapsed that distinction.", "tokens": [50930, 467, 15107, 257, 4001, 4134, 11, 457, 264, 22743, 24578, 300, 16844, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14622793197631836, "compression_ratio": 1.5350877192982457, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796981778226638e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 139762, "start": 1413.84, "end": 1417.62, "text": " The fast tempo and the slow tempo were aliased to sound identical.", "tokens": [51176, 440, 2370, 8972, 293, 264, 2964, 8972, 645, 10198, 1937, 281, 1626, 14800, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14622793197631836, "compression_ratio": 1.5350877192982457, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796981778226638e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 141762, "start": 1417.62, "end": 1419.08, "text": " So the drummer doesn't speed up.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 38535, 1177, 380, 3073, 493, 13, 50438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 141762, "start": 1419.34, "end": 1419.4199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50451, 1779, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 141762, "start": 1419.6599999999999, "end": 1425.1599999999999, "text": " The drummer has no way of knowing their reality was flattened, so they keep playing slow, and the song train racks.", "tokens": [50467, 440, 38535, 575, 572, 636, 295, 5276, 641, 4103, 390, 24183, 292, 11, 370, 436, 1066, 2433, 2964, 11, 293, 264, 2153, 3847, 47063, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 141762, "start": 1425.52, "end": 1426.4799999999998, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50760, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 141762, "start": 1427.28, "end": 1429.1599999999999, "text": " The system didn't just hide information.", "tokens": [50848, 440, 1185, 994, 380, 445, 6479, 1589, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 141762, "start": 1429.6599999999999, "end": 1431.8999999999999, "text": " It actively hallucinated a false stability.", "tokens": [50967, 467, 13022, 35212, 5410, 257, 7908, 11826, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 141762, "start": 1432.1399999999999, "end": 1432.3999999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51091, 1079, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 141762, "start": 1432.6599999999999, "end": 1438.4199999999998, "text": " And that mechanism aliasing leads directly to what Fliction calls the descent into the hall of mirrors.", "tokens": [51117, 400, 300, 7513, 10198, 3349, 6689, 3838, 281, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 264, 23475, 666, 264, 6500, 295, 24238, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 141762, "start": 1438.4799999999998, "end": 1438.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51408, 1779, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21244519166272097, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.860646836257529e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 143862, "start": 1438.62, "end": 1439.62, "text": " This is where it gets dark.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 2877, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23051493285132235, "compression_ratio": 1.4630872483221478, "no_speech_prob": 1.980633322282155e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 143862, "start": 1439.78, "end": 1445.54, "text": " Fliction decals this architectural sequence where a healthy system mutates into a toxic one.", "tokens": [50423, 3235, 4105, 979, 1124, 341, 26621, 8310, 689, 257, 4627, 1185, 5839, 1024, 666, 257, 12786, 472, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23051493285132235, "compression_ratio": 1.4630872483221478, "no_speech_prob": 1.980633322282155e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 143862, "start": 1446.4799999999998, "end": 1450.9199999999998, "text": " In a healthy system, the shared state, the room, generates a mix for the user.", "tokens": [50758, 682, 257, 4627, 1185, 11, 264, 5507, 1785, 11, 264, 1808, 11, 23815, 257, 2890, 337, 264, 4195, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23051493285132235, "compression_ratio": 1.4630872483221478, "no_speech_prob": 1.980633322282155e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 143862, "start": 1451.34, "end": 1452.54, "text": " S goes to M sub J.", "tokens": [51001, 318, 1709, 281, 376, 1422, 508, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23051493285132235, "compression_ratio": 1.4630872483221478, "no_speech_prob": 1.980633322282155e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 145254, "start": 1452.54, "end": 1461.46, "text": " But in a failing system, instead of constantly referring back to the room, the system starts building the next projection off the previous projection.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 257, 18223, 1185, 11, 2602, 295, 6460, 13761, 646, 281, 264, 1808, 11, 264, 1185, 3719, 2390, 264, 958, 22743, 766, 264, 3894, 22743, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 145254, "start": 1461.98, "end": 1464.22, "text": " It feeds its own output back into its input.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 23712, 1080, 1065, 5598, 646, 666, 1080, 4846, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 145254, "start": 1464.46, "end": 1465.96, "text": " It's the snake eating its own tail.", "tokens": [50961, 467, 311, 264, 12650, 3936, 1080, 1065, 6838, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 145254, "start": 1466.44, "end": 1467.18, "text": " Why does this happen?", "tokens": [51060, 1545, 775, 341, 1051, 30, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 145254, "start": 1467.76, "end": 1474.32, "text": " It happens because locally, step by step, it feels to the system designers like a highly efficient optimization.", "tokens": [51126, 467, 2314, 570, 16143, 11, 1823, 538, 1823, 11, 309, 3417, 281, 264, 1185, 16196, 411, 257, 5405, 7148, 19618, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 145254, "start": 1474.6599999999999, "end": 1474.98, "text": " Awesome.", "tokens": [51471, 10391, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 145254, "start": 1475.36, "end": 1478.7, "text": " Think about a recommendation algorithm on a social video platform.", "tokens": [51506, 6557, 466, 257, 11879, 9284, 322, 257, 2093, 960, 3663, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375089116615824, "compression_ratio": 1.6431226765799256, "no_speech_prob": 1.973632628854416e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 147870, "start": 1478.7, "end": 1483.14, "text": " On day one, it watches what you click on, and it builds tomorrow's feed based on those clicks.", "tokens": [50365, 1282, 786, 472, 11, 309, 17062, 437, 291, 2052, 322, 11, 293, 309, 15182, 4153, 311, 3154, 2361, 322, 729, 18521, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 147870, "start": 1483.22, "end": 1483.5800000000002, "text": " Okay, fine.", "tokens": [50591, 1033, 11, 2489, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 147870, "start": 1483.7, "end": 1483.8, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50615, 4894, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 147870, "start": 1483.96, "end": 1489.5800000000002, "text": " But then it builds the next day's feed based on how you interacted with the feed it explicitly designed for you.", "tokens": [50628, 583, 550, 309, 15182, 264, 958, 786, 311, 3154, 2361, 322, 577, 291, 49621, 365, 264, 3154, 309, 20803, 4761, 337, 291, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 147870, "start": 1489.66, "end": 1490.3600000000001, "text": " Oh, I see it.", "tokens": [50913, 876, 11, 286, 536, 309, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 147870, "start": 1490.54, "end": 1493.52, "text": " It is no longer projecting the shared state of the world.", "tokens": [50957, 467, 307, 572, 2854, 43001, 264, 5507, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 147870, "start": 1494.02, "end": 1497.46, "text": " It is projecting your reaction to its previous projection.", "tokens": [51131, 467, 307, 43001, 428, 5480, 281, 1080, 3894, 22743, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 147870, "start": 1497.68, "end": 1499.02, "text": " It's losing the tethered S.", "tokens": [51314, 467, 311, 7027, 264, 256, 1666, 292, 318, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 147870, "start": 1499.2, "end": 1499.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51390, 7587, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310108184814453, "compression_ratio": 1.6794871794871795, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102602107617714e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 149964, "start": 1499.64, "end": 1509.22, "text": " It is refining itself based entirely on your past behavior within the closed loop, not on the objective state of external reality.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 1895, 1760, 2564, 2361, 7696, 322, 428, 1791, 5223, 1951, 264, 5395, 6367, 11, 406, 322, 264, 10024, 1785, 295, 8320, 4103, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1426260688088157, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.42713727120658e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 149964, "start": 1509.7, "end": 1516.8400000000001, "text": " So locally, to a product manager looking at a chart, it feels like the system is getting more tailored, more useful, more engaging.", "tokens": [50868, 407, 16143, 11, 281, 257, 1674, 6598, 1237, 412, 257, 6927, 11, 309, 3417, 411, 264, 1185, 307, 1242, 544, 34858, 11, 544, 4420, 11, 544, 11268, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1426260688088157, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.42713727120658e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 149964, "start": 1517.14, "end": 1520.94, "text": " But globally, the shared reality vanishes completely.", "tokens": [51240, 583, 18958, 11, 264, 5507, 4103, 3161, 16423, 2584, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1426260688088157, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.42713727120658e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 149964, "start": 1521.2, "end": 1524.92, "text": " This raises an important question, though, because this is the invisible failure.", "tokens": [51443, 639, 19658, 364, 1021, 1168, 11, 1673, 11, 570, 341, 307, 264, 14603, 7763, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1426260688088157, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.42713727120658e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 152492, "start": 1524.92, "end": 1527.3400000000001, "text": " A hall of monitors has windows.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 6500, 295, 26518, 575, 9309, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 152492, "start": 1527.8200000000002, "end": 1529.52, "text": " You can look through your mix and see the room.", "tokens": [50510, 509, 393, 574, 807, 428, 2890, 293, 536, 264, 1808, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 152492, "start": 1530.1000000000001, "end": 1533.2, "text": " A hall of mirrors only has surfaces reflecting surfaces.", "tokens": [50624, 316, 6500, 295, 24238, 787, 575, 16130, 23543, 16130, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 152492, "start": 1533.72, "end": 1537.92, "text": " Your feed reflects your past choices, which reflects your past choices infinitely.", "tokens": [50805, 2260, 3154, 18926, 428, 1791, 7994, 11, 597, 18926, 428, 1791, 7994, 36227, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 152492, "start": 1538.74, "end": 1542.5800000000002, "text": " And the most terrifying part of this architecture, you cannot tell you were inside it.", "tokens": [51056, 400, 264, 881, 18106, 644, 295, 341, 9482, 11, 291, 2644, 980, 291, 645, 1854, 309, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 152492, "start": 1542.6000000000001, "end": 1543.3600000000001, "text": " No, you can't.", "tokens": [51249, 883, 11, 291, 393, 380, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 152492, "start": 1543.5, "end": 1546.74, "text": " There is no alarm bell that rings when a monitor degrades into a mirror.", "tokens": [51294, 821, 307, 572, 14183, 4549, 300, 11136, 562, 257, 6002, 368, 22626, 666, 257, 8013, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 152492, "start": 1547.0800000000002, "end": 1549.38, "text": " You don't feel a sudden sense of isolation.", "tokens": [51473, 509, 500, 380, 841, 257, 3990, 2020, 295, 16001, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 152492, "start": 1549.9, "end": 1554.7, "text": " In fact, it feels incredibly comfortable because the environment is perfectly molded to your prejudices.", "tokens": [51614, 682, 1186, 11, 309, 3417, 6252, 4619, 570, 264, 2823, 307, 6239, 11102, 292, 281, 428, 23121, 1473, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12720757997952975, "compression_ratio": 1.7572815533980584, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617221921394476e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 155470, "start": 1554.7, "end": 1555.64, "text": " It's frictionless.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 17710, 1832, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 155470, "start": 1555.98, "end": 1564.4, "text": " Yeah, you just quietly lose the capacity to ask what the actual room sounded like because the concept of the room no longer exists in your interface.", "tokens": [50429, 865, 11, 291, 445, 19141, 3624, 264, 6042, 281, 1029, 437, 264, 3539, 1808, 17714, 411, 570, 264, 3410, 295, 264, 1808, 572, 2854, 8198, 294, 428, 9226, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 155470, "start": 1564.5, "end": 1565.32, "text": " It just disappears.", "tokens": [50855, 467, 445, 25527, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 155470, "start": 1565.54, "end": 1573.76, "text": " That sends a chill down my spine because you know exactly how a tech executive from a major social platform would respond to this criticism.", "tokens": [50907, 663, 14790, 257, 11355, 760, 452, 15395, 570, 291, 458, 2293, 577, 257, 7553, 10140, 490, 257, 2563, 2093, 3663, 576, 4196, 281, 341, 15835, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 155470, "start": 1573.8400000000001, "end": 1574.4, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51322, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 155470, "start": 1574.76, "end": 1576.4, "text": " They would immediately jump on the defensive.", "tokens": [51368, 814, 576, 4258, 3012, 322, 264, 16468, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 155470, "start": 1576.5800000000002, "end": 1577.28, "text": " They'd say, wait a minute.", "tokens": [51459, 814, 1116, 584, 11, 1699, 257, 3456, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 155470, "start": 1577.76, "end": 1578.82, "text": " We are not a hall of mirrors.", "tokens": [51518, 492, 366, 406, 257, 6500, 295, 24238, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 155470, "start": 1579.16, "end": 1581.54, "text": " We keep all the original data on our servers.", "tokens": [51588, 492, 1066, 439, 264, 3380, 1412, 322, 527, 15909, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504515507182137, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.573541644206422e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 158154, "start": 1581.54, "end": 1587.8, "text": " We have flawless logs of every single post, every article, every video ever uploaded to our network.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 45693, 20820, 295, 633, 2167, 2183, 11, 633, 7222, 11, 633, 960, 1562, 17135, 281, 527, 3209, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 158154, "start": 1588.1, "end": 1589.56, "text": " We haven't lost the shared state.", "tokens": [50693, 492, 2378, 380, 2731, 264, 5507, 1785, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 158154, "start": 1589.7, "end": 1591.58, "text": " It is sitting in a data center in Oregon.", "tokens": [50773, 467, 307, 3798, 294, 257, 1412, 3056, 294, 18664, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 158154, "start": 1591.86, "end": 1592.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50881, 7587, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 158154, "start": 1592.68, "end": 1598.78, "text": " And what I love about this essay is that Fliction anticipates this exact defense and dismantles it entirely.", "tokens": [50922, 400, 437, 286, 959, 466, 341, 16238, 307, 300, 3235, 4105, 10416, 1024, 341, 1900, 7654, 293, 30506, 904, 309, 7696, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 158154, "start": 1599.0, "end": 1600.84, "text": " It is a profound dismantling.", "tokens": [51238, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 30506, 1688, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 158154, "start": 1601.0, "end": 1605.78, "text": " Fliction introduces a crucial distinction here, referencing a companion essay they wrote.", "tokens": [51338, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 11462, 16844, 510, 11, 40582, 257, 22363, 16238, 436, 4114, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 158154, "start": 1606.18, "end": 1609.84, "text": " Retained by the system is not equal to recoverable by the participant.", "tokens": [51597, 11495, 3563, 538, 264, 1185, 307, 406, 2681, 281, 8114, 712, 538, 264, 24950, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270370564909063, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.9427426247581314e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 160984, "start": 1609.84, "end": 1613.86, "text": " Let me push back on you here just to play out the tech executive's argument.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 2944, 646, 322, 291, 510, 445, 281, 862, 484, 264, 7553, 10140, 311, 6770, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 160984, "start": 1614.06, "end": 1614.76, "text": " Sure, go for it.", "tokens": [50576, 4894, 11, 352, 337, 309, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 160984, "start": 1614.9399999999998, "end": 1621.02, "text": " Because logically, if a platform has a perfect, incorruptible internal log of the shared state,", "tokens": [50620, 1436, 38887, 11, 498, 257, 3663, 575, 257, 2176, 11, 7121, 5428, 964, 6920, 3565, 295, 264, 5507, 1785, 11, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 160984, "start": 1621.1399999999999, "end": 1627.1, "text": " why does it matter if the end user can't easily see the raw chronological firehose of data?", "tokens": [50930, 983, 775, 309, 1871, 498, 264, 917, 4195, 393, 380, 3612, 536, 264, 8936, 19393, 4383, 2610, 71, 541, 295, 1412, 30, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 160984, "start": 1627.1999999999998, "end": 1627.4599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51233, 1779, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 160984, "start": 1627.82, "end": 1630.32, "text": " The objective truth still exists on the server.", "tokens": [51264, 440, 10024, 3494, 920, 8198, 322, 264, 7154, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 160984, "start": 1630.76, "end": 1633.0, "text": " The algorithm is just organizing it to be helpful.", "tokens": [51411, 440, 9284, 307, 445, 17608, 309, 281, 312, 4961, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 160984, "start": 1633.48, "end": 1634.36, "text": " It hasn't been deleted.", "tokens": [51547, 467, 6132, 380, 668, 22981, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 160984, "start": 1634.74, "end": 1637.6599999999999, "text": " It matters because of a concept called epistemic fragmentation.", "tokens": [51610, 467, 7001, 570, 295, 257, 3410, 1219, 2388, 468, 3438, 9241, 19631, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599256591796875, "compression_ratio": 1.5780730897009967, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858819249134348e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 163766, "start": 1637.66, "end": 1643.52, "text": " A system can be a perfect archive and simultaneously a terrible haul of coordination.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1185, 393, 312, 257, 2176, 23507, 293, 16561, 257, 6237, 21167, 295, 21252, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 163766, "start": 1644.0, "end": 1644.78, "text": " How does that work?", "tokens": [50682, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 30, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 163766, "start": 1645.24, "end": 1650.88, "text": " Well, if the platform has superb internal recoverability, meaning their engineers can run a SQL query", "tokens": [50744, 1042, 11, 498, 264, 3663, 575, 36617, 6920, 8114, 2310, 11, 3620, 641, 11955, 393, 1190, 257, 19200, 14581, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 163766, "start": 1650.88, "end": 1655.5800000000002, "text": " and see the raw data, but zero external recoverability for the user,", "tokens": [51026, 293, 536, 264, 8936, 1412, 11, 457, 4018, 8320, 8114, 2310, 337, 264, 4195, 11, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 163766, "start": 1655.98, "end": 1658.72, "text": " you leave the participant utterly trapped in their projection.", "tokens": [51281, 291, 1856, 264, 24950, 30251, 14994, 294, 641, 22743, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 163766, "start": 1658.8400000000001, "end": 1660.3600000000001, "text": " Because they can't access it themselves.", "tokens": [51424, 1436, 436, 393, 380, 2105, 309, 2969, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 163766, "start": 1660.6200000000001, "end": 1665.8000000000002, "text": " The user has no independent structural position from which to measure their own drift from reality.", "tokens": [51513, 440, 4195, 575, 572, 6695, 15067, 2535, 490, 597, 281, 3481, 641, 1065, 19699, 490, 4103, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11757520039876303, "compression_ratio": 1.6271186440677967, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272713870153164e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 166580, "start": 1665.8, "end": 1671.36, "text": " If I cannot practically access the raw feed to see how my personalized feed differs from it,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 2644, 15667, 2105, 264, 8936, 3154, 281, 536, 577, 452, 28415, 3154, 37761, 490, 309, 11, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 166580, "start": 1671.48, "end": 1674.3799999999999, "text": " then my personalized feed is my entire functional world.", "tokens": [50649, 550, 452, 28415, 3154, 307, 452, 2302, 11745, 1002, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 166580, "start": 1674.56, "end": 1675.46, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [50803, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 166580, "start": 1675.86, "end": 1681.98, "text": " The fact that the truth exists on a server in Oregon is entirely mathematically useless", "tokens": [50868, 440, 1186, 300, 264, 3494, 8198, 322, 257, 7154, 294, 18664, 307, 7696, 44003, 14115, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 166580, "start": 1681.98, "end": 1685.3999999999999, "text": " to my ability to coordinate my actions with my fellow citizens.", "tokens": [51174, 281, 452, 3485, 281, 15670, 452, 5909, 365, 452, 7177, 7180, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 166580, "start": 1686.1399999999999, "end": 1689.12, "text": " The system hoards the truth for its own oversight,", "tokens": [51382, 440, 1185, 1106, 2287, 264, 3494, 337, 1080, 1065, 29146, 11, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 166580, "start": 1689.6, "end": 1692.8799999999999, "text": " but denies the user the navigational tools to find it.", "tokens": [51555, 457, 1441, 530, 264, 4195, 264, 7407, 1478, 3873, 281, 915, 309, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13825742721557618, "compression_ratio": 1.7103174603174602, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 169288, "start": 1692.88, "end": 1698.46, "text": " The analogy that came to mind here is the difference between a public library and a prison cell with a book slot.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 21663, 300, 1361, 281, 1575, 510, 307, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 1908, 6405, 293, 257, 6168, 2815, 365, 257, 1446, 14747, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 169288, "start": 1699.0600000000002, "end": 1700.18, "text": " Oh, that's dark, but yeah.", "tokens": [50674, 876, 11, 300, 311, 2877, 11, 457, 1338, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 169288, "start": 1700.2800000000002, "end": 1703.5, "text": " In a public library, I might spend all my time in the science fiction section.", "tokens": [50735, 682, 257, 1908, 6405, 11, 286, 1062, 3496, 439, 452, 565, 294, 264, 3497, 13266, 3541, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 169288, "start": 1703.64, "end": 1705.1200000000001, "text": " That's my preference, my projection.", "tokens": [50903, 663, 311, 452, 17502, 11, 452, 22743, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 169288, "start": 1705.6000000000001, "end": 1712.6200000000001, "text": " But I can physically stand up, look across the room, and see the biography section, the history section, the reference desk.", "tokens": [51001, 583, 286, 393, 9762, 1463, 493, 11, 574, 2108, 264, 1808, 11, 293, 536, 264, 37062, 3541, 11, 264, 2503, 3541, 11, 264, 6408, 10026, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 169288, "start": 1712.8200000000002, "end": 1715.2, "text": " You have a map of the total shared state.", "tokens": [51362, 509, 362, 257, 4471, 295, 264, 3217, 5507, 1785, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10579021846022561, "compression_ratio": 1.692, "no_speech_prob": 2.4089183339043307e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 171520, "start": 1715.2, "end": 1721.3400000000001, "text": " Exactly. The modern tech platform is like being locked in a room where a librarian slides books under the door", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 4363, 7553, 3663, 307, 411, 885, 9376, 294, 257, 1808, 689, 257, 42558, 9788, 3642, 833, 264, 2853, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 171520, "start": 1721.3400000000001, "end": 1723.54, "text": " based purely on what you read yesterday.", "tokens": [50672, 2361, 17491, 322, 437, 291, 1401, 5186, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 171520, "start": 1723.68, "end": 1724.94, "text": " That is precisely the difference.", "tokens": [50789, 663, 307, 13402, 264, 2649, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 171520, "start": 1725.06, "end": 1727.68, "text": " The books exist. The library building exists.", "tokens": [50858, 440, 3642, 2514, 13, 440, 6405, 2390, 8198, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 171520, "start": 1728.26, "end": 1729.7, "text": " But you have no map of it.", "tokens": [51018, 583, 291, 362, 572, 4471, 295, 309, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 171520, "start": 1729.8, "end": 1732.64, "text": " You have no way to verify if history books even exist anymore.", "tokens": [51095, 509, 362, 572, 636, 281, 16888, 498, 2503, 3642, 754, 2514, 3602, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 171520, "start": 1732.8400000000001, "end": 1733.18, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51247, 1079, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 171520, "start": 1733.68, "end": 1737.24, "text": " Infliction contrasts the systemic failure with the companion essay.", "tokens": [51289, 682, 3423, 4105, 8712, 82, 264, 23789, 7763, 365, 264, 22363, 16238, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 171520, "start": 1737.7, "end": 1743.24, "text": " That earlier essay was about how a single individual might lose their way in a mediated reality.", "tokens": [51490, 663, 3071, 16238, 390, 466, 577, 257, 2167, 2609, 1062, 3624, 641, 636, 294, 257, 17269, 770, 4103, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12097409192253561, "compression_ratio": 1.6815068493150684, "no_speech_prob": 1.655501148493943e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 174324, "start": 1743.24, "end": 1745.36, "text": " But this essay is about architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 341, 16238, 307, 466, 9482, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 174324, "start": 1745.84, "end": 1748.6200000000001, "text": " It's about the literal floor plan of the system itself.", "tokens": [50495, 467, 311, 466, 264, 20411, 4123, 1393, 295, 264, 1185, 2564, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 174324, "start": 1749.42, "end": 1749.74, "text": " The blueprint.", "tokens": [50674, 440, 35868, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 174324, "start": 1749.96, "end": 1753.92, "text": " The question is, did the architects ever build way home in the first place?", "tokens": [50701, 440, 1168, 307, 11, 630, 264, 30491, 1562, 1322, 636, 1280, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 30, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 174324, "start": 1754.24, "end": 1758.28, "text": " If the route back to the shared state isn't practically available to the participant,", "tokens": [50915, 759, 264, 7955, 646, 281, 264, 5507, 1785, 1943, 380, 15667, 2435, 281, 264, 24950, 11, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 174324, "start": 1758.72, "end": 1762.68, "text": " if the UI hides it, if the algorithm actively suppresses it,", "tokens": [51139, 498, 264, 15682, 35953, 309, 11, 498, 264, 9284, 13022, 26835, 279, 309, 11, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 174324, "start": 1762.86, "end": 1765.48, "text": " then the architecture is fundamentally a hall of mirrors,", "tokens": [51346, 550, 264, 9482, 307, 17879, 257, 6500, 295, 24238, 11, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 174324, "start": 1765.84, "end": 1769.02, "text": " regardless of how many petabytes of data they retain on their back end.", "tokens": [51495, 10060, 295, 577, 867, 3817, 24538, 295, 1412, 436, 18340, 322, 641, 646, 917, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16065819199020798, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271352112224522e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 176902, "start": 1769.02, "end": 1775.98, "text": " Okay, so if we accept that giving everyone access to a recoverable reality is the goal of a good system,", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 321, 3241, 300, 2902, 1518, 2105, 281, 257, 8114, 712, 4103, 307, 264, 3387, 295, 257, 665, 1185, 11, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 176902, "start": 1776.26, "end": 1778.76, "text": " we run into a massive logistical problem.", "tokens": [50727, 321, 1190, 666, 257, 5994, 3565, 42686, 1154, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 176902, "start": 1779.08, "end": 1779.5, "text": " What's that?", "tokens": [50868, 708, 311, 300, 30, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 176902, "start": 1779.8799999999999, "end": 1783.4, "text": " How does a system decide who gets what specific mix to begin with?", "tokens": [50908, 1012, 775, 257, 1185, 4536, 567, 2170, 437, 2685, 2890, 281, 1841, 365, 30, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 176902, "start": 1783.68, "end": 1785.52, "text": " How do you construct the initial projection?", "tokens": [51098, 1012, 360, 291, 7690, 264, 5883, 22743, 30, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 176902, "start": 1786.74, "end": 1792.26, "text": " According to Fliction, system designers are completely conflating two entirely different computational problems.", "tokens": [51251, 7328, 281, 3235, 4105, 11, 1185, 16196, 366, 2584, 1497, 75, 990, 732, 7696, 819, 28270, 2740, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15728587044609918, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.883259173607321e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 179226, "start": 1792.26, "end": 1798.08, "text": " This is perhaps the most practical, actionable insight in the entire piece for anyone building software.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 8496, 11, 45098, 11269, 294, 264, 2302, 2522, 337, 2878, 2390, 4722, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 179226, "start": 1798.62, "end": 1802.86, "text": " There are two distinct scheduling problems in any collaborative environment,", "tokens": [50683, 821, 366, 732, 10644, 29055, 2740, 294, 604, 16555, 2823, 11, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 179226, "start": 1803.22, "end": 1805.08, "text": " and naive systems smash them together.", "tokens": [50913, 293, 29052, 3652, 17960, 552, 1214, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 179226, "start": 1805.36, "end": 1806.48, "text": " Production and perception.", "tokens": [51020, 30088, 293, 12860, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 179226, "start": 1806.7, "end": 1807.96, "text": " Let's break those down deeply.", "tokens": [51087, 961, 311, 1821, 729, 760, 8760, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 179226, "start": 1808.76, "end": 1813.5, "text": " First, production, which the essay denotes as the graph of production.", "tokens": [51190, 2386, 11, 4265, 11, 597, 264, 16238, 1441, 17251, 382, 264, 4295, 295, 4265, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 179226, "start": 1813.72, "end": 1818.32, "text": " This is simply about who realizes which component of the shared state.", "tokens": [51438, 639, 307, 2935, 466, 567, 29316, 597, 6542, 295, 264, 5507, 1785, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16176537105015346, "compression_ratio": 1.6091954022988506, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 181832, "start": 1818.32, "end": 1818.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 181832, "start": 1819.0, "end": 1820.2, "text": " Who plays the guitar?", "tokens": [50399, 2102, 5749, 264, 7531, 30, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 181832, "start": 1820.78, "end": 1821.8999999999999, "text": " Who sings the lead vocal?", "tokens": [50488, 2102, 23250, 264, 1477, 11657, 30, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 181832, "start": 1822.56, "end": 1824.28, "text": " Who keeps the time on the drum kit?", "tokens": [50577, 2102, 5965, 264, 565, 322, 264, 10206, 8260, 30, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 181832, "start": 1824.54, "end": 1828.96, "text": " It's an assignment problem based on affinity, skill, or resource allocation.", "tokens": [50676, 467, 311, 364, 15187, 1154, 2361, 322, 39703, 11, 5389, 11, 420, 7684, 27599, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 181832, "start": 1829.46, "end": 1835.1599999999999, "text": " You assign the drum part to the person who has the physical stamina and rhythmic skill to play the drums.", "tokens": [50922, 509, 6269, 264, 10206, 644, 281, 264, 954, 567, 575, 264, 4001, 36690, 293, 46967, 5389, 281, 862, 264, 20420, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 181832, "start": 1835.28, "end": 1835.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51213, 1779, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 181832, "start": 1835.62, "end": 1836.78, "text": " It's the division of labor.", "tokens": [51230, 467, 311, 264, 10044, 295, 5938, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 181832, "start": 1836.96, "end": 1839.6399999999999, "text": " It answers the question, who is generating the signal?", "tokens": [51297, 467, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 567, 307, 17746, 264, 6358, 30, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 181832, "start": 1839.8, "end": 1840.6, "text": " And the other graph.", "tokens": [51439, 400, 264, 661, 4295, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 181832, "start": 1840.72, "end": 1843.28, "text": " But then you have the completely separate graph of perception.", "tokens": [51485, 583, 550, 291, 362, 264, 2584, 4994, 4295, 295, 12860, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611334913868015, "compression_ratio": 1.661710037174721, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465673868456323e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 184328, "start": 1843.28, "end": 1848.42, "text": " This answers the question, who needs to perceive which component in order to do their job well?", "tokens": [50365, 639, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 567, 2203, 281, 20281, 597, 6542, 294, 1668, 281, 360, 641, 1691, 731, 30, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 184328, "start": 1848.74, "end": 1857.24, "text": " And the fatal conflation is that most naive personalization software, especially early machine learning models, collapses these two graphs into one.", "tokens": [50638, 400, 264, 24069, 1497, 24278, 307, 300, 881, 29052, 2973, 2144, 4722, 11, 2318, 2440, 3479, 2539, 5245, 11, 48765, 613, 732, 24877, 666, 472, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 184328, "start": 1857.3799999999999, "end": 1857.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51070, 7587, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 184328, "start": 1858.2, "end": 1863.02, "text": " The algorithm assumes that whoever is producing a signal must be the one who most needs to perceive it.", "tokens": [51111, 440, 9284, 37808, 300, 11387, 307, 10501, 257, 6358, 1633, 312, 264, 472, 567, 881, 2203, 281, 20281, 309, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 184328, "start": 1863.2, "end": 1868.5, "text": " Which, if we go back to our master metaphor of the stage, is demonstrably hilariously false.", "tokens": [51361, 3013, 11, 498, 321, 352, 646, 281, 527, 4505, 19157, 295, 264, 3233, 11, 307, 5516, 5305, 356, 18661, 8994, 7908, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 184328, "start": 1868.66, "end": 1869.0, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51634, 467, 307, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 184328, "start": 1869.16, "end": 1871.26, "text": " The drummer does not sing the lead vocal line.", "tokens": [51659, 440, 38535, 775, 406, 1522, 264, 1477, 11657, 1622, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11036940752449682, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886469014609548e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 187126, "start": 1871.26, "end": 1873.56, "text": " The drummer is not producing that signal.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 38535, 307, 406, 10501, 300, 6358, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 187126, "start": 1874.3, "end": 1882.04, "text": " But the drummer absolutely desperately needs to hear the vocal line in their monitor to understand the macro structure of the song.", "tokens": [50517, 583, 264, 38535, 3122, 23726, 2203, 281, 1568, 264, 11657, 1622, 294, 641, 6002, 281, 1223, 264, 18887, 3877, 295, 264, 2153, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 187126, "start": 1882.24, "end": 1882.54, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50914, 1079, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 187126, "start": 1882.94, "end": 1889.5, "text": " If you collapse production and perception, the algorithm would say, well, the singer is producing vocals, so only feed vocals to the singer.", "tokens": [50949, 759, 291, 15584, 4265, 293, 12860, 11, 264, 9284, 576, 584, 11, 731, 11, 264, 11564, 307, 10501, 28441, 11, 370, 787, 3154, 28441, 281, 264, 11564, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 187126, "start": 1889.72, "end": 1893.64, "text": " The drummer is producing percussion, so only feed percussion to the drummer.", "tokens": [51288, 440, 38535, 307, 10501, 44430, 11, 370, 787, 3154, 44430, 281, 264, 38535, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 187126, "start": 1893.92, "end": 1899.1, "text": " The band would collapse into total rhythmic chaos in less than 10 seconds.", "tokens": [51498, 440, 4116, 576, 15584, 666, 3217, 46967, 14158, 294, 1570, 813, 1266, 3949, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 187126, "start": 1899.2, "end": 1899.72, "text": " Instantly.", "tokens": [51762, 2730, 3627, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 187126, "start": 1899.72, "end": 1900.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51788, 1033, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 187126, "start": 1900.26, "end": 1900.86, "text": " I love this.", "tokens": [51815, 286, 959, 341, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14669534715555482, "compression_ratio": 1.835164835164835, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132566423894933e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 190086, "start": 1900.86, "end": 1913.1799999999998, "text": " And I want to dive into the exact mechanics of how you solve this perception problem, because you pull some fascinating context from the footnotes regarding how this actually works physically in the ear.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 286, 528, 281, 9192, 666, 264, 1900, 12939, 295, 577, 291, 5039, 341, 12860, 1154, 11, 570, 291, 2235, 512, 10343, 4319, 490, 264, 2671, 2247, 279, 8595, 577, 341, 767, 1985, 9762, 294, 264, 1273, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 190086, "start": 1913.36, "end": 1914.2199999999998, "text": " Yeah, I did.", "tokens": [50990, 865, 11, 286, 630, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 190086, "start": 1914.36, "end": 1916.82, "text": " You introduced this concept of the noise floor.", "tokens": [51040, 509, 7268, 341, 3410, 295, 264, 5658, 4123, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 190086, "start": 1917.04, "end": 1917.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51174, 1079, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 190086, "start": 1917.74, "end": 1922.86, "text": " This is where flixing gets incredibly granular, but it's essential for understanding why algorithms fail.", "tokens": [51209, 639, 307, 689, 932, 970, 278, 2170, 6252, 39962, 11, 457, 309, 311, 7115, 337, 3701, 983, 14642, 3061, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 190086, "start": 1923.26, "end": 1927.84, "text": " Every participant in a system has a local detection threshold known as a noise floor.", "tokens": [51485, 2048, 24950, 294, 257, 1185, 575, 257, 2654, 17784, 14678, 2570, 382, 257, 5658, 4123, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 190086, "start": 1928.04, "end": 1928.76, "text": " A noise floor.", "tokens": [51724, 316, 5658, 4123, 13, 51760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10846490859985351, "compression_ratio": 1.6357388316151202, "no_speech_prob": 2.193352487481204e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 192876, "start": 1928.76, "end": 1931.28, "text": " Below that floor, a signal might be physically real.", "tokens": [50365, 36261, 300, 4123, 11, 257, 6358, 1062, 312, 9762, 957, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 192876, "start": 1931.4, "end": 1935.92, "text": " It might be transmitted perfectly by the system, but it doesn't exist cognitively to that person.", "tokens": [50497, 467, 1062, 312, 25355, 6239, 538, 264, 1185, 11, 457, 309, 1177, 380, 2514, 15605, 356, 281, 300, 954, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 192876, "start": 1936.14, "end": 1945.66, "text": " So if the vocal line is playing in the drummer's monitor, but it's below their noise floor because the bass is so loud, the drummer cannot use it to keep time.", "tokens": [50734, 407, 498, 264, 11657, 1622, 307, 2433, 294, 264, 38535, 311, 6002, 11, 457, 309, 311, 2507, 641, 5658, 4123, 570, 264, 10136, 307, 370, 6588, 11, 264, 38535, 2644, 764, 309, 281, 1066, 565, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 192876, "start": 1945.86, "end": 1947.46, "text": " It is functionally non-existent.", "tokens": [51220, 467, 307, 2445, 379, 2107, 12, 18217, 317, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 192876, "start": 1947.54, "end": 1947.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51304, 7587, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 192876, "start": 1948.34, "end": 1949.84, "text": " I want to make sure I understand this mechanically.", "tokens": [51344, 286, 528, 281, 652, 988, 286, 1223, 341, 4236, 984, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 192876, "start": 1950.18, "end": 1953.68, "text": " Let's say I'm the sound engineer, and the drummer says, I can't hear the singer.", "tokens": [51436, 961, 311, 584, 286, 478, 264, 1626, 11403, 11, 293, 264, 38535, 1619, 11, 286, 393, 380, 1568, 264, 11564, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202750357370528, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370913092685456e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 195368, "start": 1953.68, "end": 1958.26, "text": " My instinct is just to grab the master volume knob and turn everything up.", "tokens": [50365, 1222, 16556, 307, 445, 281, 4444, 264, 4505, 5523, 26759, 293, 1261, 1203, 493, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 195368, "start": 1958.5, "end": 1958.68, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50606, 4894, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 195368, "start": 1958.8600000000001, "end": 1960.8400000000001, "text": " Make the whole mix uniformly louder.", "tokens": [50624, 4387, 264, 1379, 2890, 48806, 22717, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 195368, "start": 1961.3, "end": 1963.5600000000002, "text": " But you're saying that doesn't fix the problem.", "tokens": [50746, 583, 291, 434, 1566, 300, 1177, 380, 3191, 264, 1154, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 195368, "start": 1963.78, "end": 1967.44, "text": " It absolutely does not fix the problem, and in fact, it usually makes it worse.", "tokens": [50870, 467, 3122, 775, 406, 3191, 264, 1154, 11, 293, 294, 1186, 11, 309, 2673, 1669, 309, 5324, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 195368, "start": 1967.68, "end": 1967.94, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [51065, 1545, 30, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20887554555699445, "compression_ratio": 1.4204545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.279407786311526e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 196794, "start": 1967.94, "end": 1973.46, "text": " Because if you just crank the master volume, you raise the noise floor along with the signal.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 445, 21263, 264, 4505, 5523, 11, 291, 5300, 264, 5658, 4123, 2051, 365, 264, 6358, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 196794, "start": 1973.72, "end": 1976.6200000000001, "text": " You make the bass louder, the click track louder, the vocal louder.", "tokens": [50654, 509, 652, 264, 10136, 22717, 11, 264, 2052, 2837, 22717, 11, 264, 11657, 22717, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 196794, "start": 1976.92, "end": 1980.16, "text": " The vocal is still buried underneath the competing frequencies.", "tokens": [50814, 440, 11657, 307, 920, 14101, 7223, 264, 15439, 20250, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 196794, "start": 1980.42, "end": 1982.5800000000002, "text": " It's just vibrating the eardrum harder.", "tokens": [50989, 467, 311, 445, 47748, 264, 308, 515, 6247, 6081, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 196794, "start": 1982.5800000000002, "end": 1983.02, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51097, 2438, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 196794, "start": 1983.74, "end": 1986.7, "text": " You just deafen the musician without providing any clarity.", "tokens": [51155, 509, 445, 15559, 268, 264, 19570, 1553, 6530, 604, 16992, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 196794, "start": 1987.38, "end": 1989.98, "text": " So perception routing isn't about volume.", "tokens": [51337, 407, 12860, 32722, 1943, 380, 466, 5523, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 196794, "start": 1990.6200000000001, "end": 1992.92, "text": " It's about selective threshold manipulation.", "tokens": [51499, 467, 311, 466, 33930, 14678, 26475, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21139732360839844, "compression_ratio": 1.6706827309236947, "no_speech_prob": 1.5241529826431899e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 199292, "start": 1993.74, "end": 1994.3000000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50406, 7587, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 199292, "start": 1994.6200000000001, "end": 2000.46, "text": " It's about intelligently raising a very specific signal, like the vocal cue, just enough to", "tokens": [50450, 467, 311, 466, 5613, 2276, 11225, 257, 588, 2685, 6358, 11, 411, 264, 11657, 22656, 11, 445, 1547, 281, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 199292, "start": 2000.46, "end": 2005.0800000000002, "text": " cross the drummer's specific threshold of perception at a specific moment in the song", "tokens": [50742, 3278, 264, 38535, 311, 2685, 14678, 295, 12860, 412, 257, 2685, 1623, 294, 264, 2153, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 199292, "start": 2005.0800000000002, "end": 2009.3000000000002, "text": " while actively suppressing or letting other competing signals recede.", "tokens": [50973, 1339, 13022, 1003, 18605, 420, 8295, 661, 15439, 12354, 850, 4858, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 199292, "start": 2009.76, "end": 2014.42, "text": " And again, you pulled some amazing historical context from footnotes four and five about where", "tokens": [51207, 400, 797, 11, 291, 7373, 512, 2243, 8584, 4319, 490, 2671, 2247, 279, 1451, 293, 1732, 466, 689, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 199292, "start": 2014.42, "end": 2015.88, "text": " this theory actually comes from.", "tokens": [51440, 341, 5261, 767, 1487, 490, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 199292, "start": 2016.52, "end": 2020.1200000000001, "text": " Fliction is drawing on decades of intense scientific research here.", "tokens": [51545, 3235, 4105, 307, 6316, 322, 7878, 295, 9447, 8134, 2132, 510, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 199292, "start": 2020.2, "end": 2021.9, "text": " I really couldn't resist going deep on this.", "tokens": [51729, 286, 534, 2809, 380, 4597, 516, 2452, 322, 341, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14804770265306746, "compression_ratio": 1.6566666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.536840208045398e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 202190, "start": 2021.9, "end": 2026.7800000000002, "text": " Footnote 4 traces this back to human automation research from the 1970s and 1990s.", "tokens": [50365, 20989, 22178, 1017, 26076, 341, 646, 281, 1952, 17769, 2132, 490, 264, 14577, 82, 293, 13384, 82, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 202190, "start": 2026.8000000000002, "end": 2027.46, "text": " Who were the pioneers?", "tokens": [50610, 2102, 645, 264, 47381, 30, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 202190, "start": 2027.46, "end": 2031.2800000000002, "text": " People like Thomas Sheridan, Bill Verplank, and Christopher Wickens.", "tokens": [50643, 3432, 411, 8500, 11789, 31675, 11, 5477, 4281, 564, 657, 11, 293, 20649, 47702, 694, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 202190, "start": 2031.8600000000001, "end": 2036.8600000000001, "text": " They studied how to allocate tasks in high-stress environments between human operators and early", "tokens": [50863, 814, 9454, 577, 281, 35713, 9608, 294, 1090, 12, 372, 735, 12388, 1296, 1952, 19077, 293, 2440, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 202190, "start": 2036.8600000000001, "end": 2037.68, "text": " computer systems.", "tokens": [51113, 3820, 3652, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 202190, "start": 2038.5, "end": 2040.3600000000001, "text": " But Fliction points out their blind spot.", "tokens": [51195, 583, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 641, 6865, 4008, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 202190, "start": 2040.92, "end": 2046.38, "text": " Even they frequently fail to cleanly separate who produces an action from who perceives the", "tokens": [51316, 2754, 436, 10374, 3061, 281, 2541, 356, 4994, 567, 14725, 364, 3069, 490, 567, 9016, 1539, 264, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 202190, "start": 2046.38, "end": 2047.5400000000002, "text": " feedback of that action.", "tokens": [51589, 5824, 295, 300, 3069, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 202190, "start": 2047.72, "end": 2048.58, "text": " They conflated them.", "tokens": [51656, 814, 1497, 38539, 552, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713320856509, "compression_ratio": 1.5478547854785478, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139614330508e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 204858, "start": 2048.58, "end": 2051.04, "text": " Yes, they treated allocation as a single variable.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 436, 8668, 27599, 382, 257, 2167, 7006, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 204858, "start": 2051.88, "end": 2057.18, "text": " Fliction is arguing that separating those two graphs is the fundamental key to modern coordination.", "tokens": [50530, 3235, 4105, 307, 19697, 300, 29279, 729, 732, 24877, 307, 264, 8088, 2141, 281, 4363, 21252, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 204858, "start": 2057.46, "end": 2058.84, "text": " What about footnote 5?", "tokens": [50809, 708, 466, 2671, 22178, 1025, 30, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 204858, "start": 2058.94, "end": 2060.58, "text": " This was the psychoacoustic stuff, right?", "tokens": [50883, 639, 390, 264, 33355, 326, 15849, 299, 1507, 11, 558, 30, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 204858, "start": 2060.96, "end": 2061.3199999999997, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50984, 1079, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 204858, "start": 2062.0, "end": 2069.2599999999998, "text": " Footnote 5 traces the noise floor concept back to 1966, to David Green and John Swetz's signal", "tokens": [51036, 20989, 22178, 1025, 26076, 264, 5658, 4123, 3410, 646, 281, 39157, 11, 281, 4389, 6969, 293, 2619, 3926, 10074, 311, 6358, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15084820029176313, "compression_ratio": 1.40625, "no_speech_prob": 1.890638036752823e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 206926, "start": 2069.26, "end": 2075.5200000000004, "text": " detection theory, and even further back to Harvey Fletcher's groundbreaking 1933 work on critical", "tokens": [50365, 17784, 5261, 11, 293, 754, 3052, 646, 281, 28796, 479, 2631, 6759, 311, 42491, 48390, 589, 322, 4924, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 206926, "start": 2075.5200000000004, "end": 2076.0, "text": " bands.", "tokens": [50678, 13543, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 206926, "start": 2076.5, "end": 2076.9, "text": " 1933.", "tokens": [50727, 48390, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 206926, "start": 2077.2200000000003, "end": 2078.1800000000003, "text": " That's almost 100 years ago.", "tokens": [50763, 663, 311, 1920, 2319, 924, 2057, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 206926, "start": 2078.2200000000003, "end": 2078.5800000000004, "text": " I know.", "tokens": [50813, 286, 458, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 206926, "start": 2079.0400000000004, "end": 2083.0, "text": " Fletcher was a physicist at Bell Labs, and he proved mathematically that a tone isn't", "tokens": [50854, 479, 2631, 6759, 390, 257, 42466, 412, 11485, 40047, 11, 293, 415, 14617, 44003, 300, 257, 8027, 1943, 380, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 206926, "start": 2083.0, "end": 2084.5800000000004, "text": " drowned out by all the noise in a room.", "tokens": [51052, 38233, 484, 538, 439, 264, 5658, 294, 257, 1808, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 206926, "start": 2084.84, "end": 2089.5600000000004, "text": " It is only drowned out by a very narrow band of noise frequencies immediately surrounding it.", "tokens": [51144, 467, 307, 787, 38233, 484, 538, 257, 588, 9432, 4116, 295, 5658, 20250, 4258, 11498, 309, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531580686569214, "compression_ratio": 1.5165289256198347, "no_speech_prob": 2.904316977886401e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 208956, "start": 2089.56, "end": 2093.18, "text": " So if you want somebody to hear a 1,000 hertz tone, you don't need a silent room.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 291, 528, 2618, 281, 1568, 257, 502, 11, 1360, 45830, 8027, 11, 291, 500, 380, 643, 257, 12784, 1808, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 208956, "start": 2093.2999999999997, "end": 2097.32, "text": " Joe, you just need to carve out the noise between 900 and 1,100 hertz.", "tokens": [50552, 6807, 11, 291, 445, 643, 281, 33832, 484, 264, 5658, 1296, 22016, 293, 502, 11, 6879, 45830, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 208956, "start": 2097.48, "end": 2097.62, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50761, 3153, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 208956, "start": 2098.16, "end": 2104.7799999999997, "text": " Flexion is taking this incredibly specific physical acoustic phenomenon and applying it to general", "tokens": [50795, 29208, 313, 307, 1940, 341, 6252, 2685, 4001, 26753, 14029, 293, 9275, 309, 281, 2674, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 208956, "start": 2104.7799999999997, "end": 2106.7799999999997, "text": " socio-technical system architecture.", "tokens": [51126, 44303, 12, 29113, 804, 1185, 9482, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 208956, "start": 2107.2, "end": 2109.24, "text": " The algorithm doesn't need to show you everything.", "tokens": [51247, 440, 9284, 1177, 380, 643, 281, 855, 291, 1203, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 208956, "start": 2109.46, "end": 2113.94, "text": " It just needs to carve out the specific cognitive frequencies competing with the signal you need", "tokens": [51360, 467, 445, 2203, 281, 33832, 484, 264, 2685, 15605, 20250, 15439, 365, 264, 6358, 291, 643, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 208956, "start": 2113.94, "end": 2114.48, "text": " right now.", "tokens": [51584, 558, 586, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 208956, "start": 2114.7, "end": 2116.7, "text": " It is a brilliant extrapolation.", "tokens": [51622, 467, 307, 257, 10248, 48224, 399, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15341493288675945, "compression_ratio": 1.6440677966101696, "no_speech_prob": 1.996903510603776e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 211670, "start": 2116.7, "end": 2121.16, "text": " It really is. But translating that to software brings up a massive practical issue.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 583, 35030, 300, 281, 4722, 5607, 493, 257, 5994, 8496, 2734, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 211670, "start": 2121.7, "end": 2125.22, "text": " We've established we need to constantly manipulate this noise floor for each person.", "tokens": [50615, 492, 600, 7545, 321, 643, 281, 6460, 20459, 341, 5658, 4123, 337, 1184, 954, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 211670, "start": 2125.56, "end": 2127.6, "text": " But how does a system do that?", "tokens": [50808, 583, 577, 775, 257, 1185, 360, 300, 30, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 211670, "start": 2127.7, "end": 2128.08, "text": " It's hard.", "tokens": [50915, 467, 311, 1152, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 211670, "start": 2128.22, "end": 2133.2599999999998, "text": " Is this just a settings menu? Like, I open my app, check some preference boxes, say show", "tokens": [50941, 1119, 341, 445, 257, 6257, 6510, 30, 1743, 11, 286, 1269, 452, 724, 11, 1520, 512, 17502, 9002, 11, 584, 855, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 211670, "start": 2133.2599999999998, "end": 2137.8199999999997, "text": " me more news, show me less sports, and then the system just runs on autopilot forever.", "tokens": [51193, 385, 544, 2583, 11, 855, 385, 1570, 6573, 11, 293, 550, 264, 1185, 445, 6676, 322, 31090, 31516, 5680, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 211670, "start": 2138.24, "end": 2142.8199999999997, "text": " Not at all. And this is the trap that almost every modern consumer platform falls into.", "tokens": [51442, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 400, 341, 307, 264, 11487, 300, 1920, 633, 4363, 9711, 3663, 8804, 666, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 211670, "start": 2142.9399999999996, "end": 2145.06, "text": " Flexion calls this the myth of the profile.", "tokens": [51677, 29208, 313, 5498, 341, 264, 9474, 295, 264, 7964, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0991812485914964, "compression_ratio": 1.61875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6719600964137937e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 214506, "start": 2145.06, "end": 2150.82, "text": " Right. Most modern personalization works by building a static historical preference profile.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 4534, 4363, 2973, 2144, 1985, 538, 2390, 257, 13437, 8584, 17502, 7964, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10834903958477551, "compression_ratio": 1.4641350210970465, "no_speech_prob": 1.875912402846125e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 214506, "start": 2151.16, "end": 2151.42, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50670, 1079, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10834903958477551, "compression_ratio": 1.4641350210970465, "no_speech_prob": 1.875912402846125e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 214506, "start": 2151.74, "end": 2156.16, "text": " The algorithm looks at what you clicked on yesterday, last week, last month, and builds", "tokens": [50699, 440, 9284, 1542, 412, 437, 291, 23370, 322, 5186, 11, 1036, 1243, 11, 1036, 1618, 11, 293, 15182, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10834903958477551, "compression_ratio": 1.4641350210970465, "no_speech_prob": 1.875912402846125e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 214506, "start": 2156.16, "end": 2163.54, "text": " a dossier. User 405 likes cat videos, baking tutorials, and political outrage. We will weigh", "tokens": [50920, 257, 47831, 811, 13, 32127, 3356, 20, 5902, 3857, 2145, 11, 12102, 17616, 11, 293, 3905, 25933, 13, 492, 486, 13843, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10834903958477551, "compression_ratio": 1.4641350210970465, "no_speech_prob": 1.875912402846125e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 214506, "start": 2163.54, "end": 2168.02, "text": " those variables heavily and feed them exactly that cocktail forever.", "tokens": [51289, 729, 9102, 10950, 293, 3154, 552, 2293, 300, 26382, 5680, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10834903958477551, "compression_ratio": 1.4641350210970465, "no_speech_prob": 1.875912402846125e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 216802, "start": 2168.02, "end": 2172.86, "text": " But a live monitor engineer on a concert stage does not work that way. A professional monitor", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 1621, 6002, 11403, 322, 257, 8543, 3233, 775, 406, 589, 300, 636, 13, 316, 4843, 6002, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 216802, "start": 2172.86, "end": 2177.06, "text": " console is not a static profile. It is a highly dynamic instrument.", "tokens": [50607, 11076, 307, 406, 257, 13437, 7964, 13, 467, 307, 257, 5405, 8546, 7198, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 216802, "start": 2177.2, "end": 2178.08, "text": " It's constantly changing.", "tokens": [50824, 467, 311, 6460, 4473, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 216802, "start": 2178.2, "end": 2183.12, "text": " The weights of the mix are changing continuously in real time. When the singer has a really", "tokens": [50874, 440, 17443, 295, 264, 2890, 366, 4473, 15684, 294, 957, 565, 13, 1133, 264, 11564, 575, 257, 534, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 216802, "start": 2183.12, "end": 2188.08, "text": " tough, exposed vocal entrance come up in the bridge of a song, the engineer doesn't just", "tokens": [51120, 4930, 11, 9495, 11657, 12014, 808, 493, 294, 264, 7283, 295, 257, 2153, 11, 264, 11403, 1177, 380, 445, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 216802, "start": 2188.08, "end": 2193.16, "text": " leave the mix alone. The engineer might push a specific keyboard pitch reference forward", "tokens": [51368, 1856, 264, 2890, 3312, 13, 440, 11403, 1062, 2944, 257, 2685, 10186, 7293, 6408, 2128, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05721512581538228, "compression_ratio": 1.673992673992674, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071275390882155e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 219316, "start": 2193.16, "end": 2197.92, "text": " in the singer's ear for exactly three seconds leading up to the entrance. And the millisecond,", "tokens": [50365, 294, 264, 11564, 311, 1273, 337, 2293, 1045, 3949, 5775, 493, 281, 264, 12014, 13, 400, 264, 27940, 18882, 11, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 219316, "start": 2198.08, "end": 2202.8799999999997, "text": " the singer hits the note securely. The engineer pulls that keyboard back down so it doesn't", "tokens": [50611, 264, 11564, 8664, 264, 3637, 38348, 13, 440, 11403, 16982, 300, 10186, 646, 760, 370, 309, 1177, 380, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 219316, "start": 2202.8799999999997, "end": 2204.56, "text": " clutter the rest of the vocal performance.", "tokens": [50851, 40614, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 11657, 3389, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 219316, "start": 2204.7999999999997, "end": 2205.06, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50947, 883, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 219316, "start": 2205.2999999999997, "end": 2209.8999999999996, "text": " The monitor responds to the demands of the present moment and the requirements of the immediate", "tokens": [50972, 440, 6002, 27331, 281, 264, 15107, 295, 264, 1974, 1623, 293, 264, 7728, 295, 264, 11629, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 219316, "start": 2209.8999999999996, "end": 2214.3799999999997, "text": " future, not a historical average of what the singer listened to last week.", "tokens": [51202, 2027, 11, 406, 257, 8584, 4274, 295, 437, 264, 11564, 13207, 281, 1036, 1243, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15320063150057228, "compression_ratio": 1.6974789915966386, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564814419289584e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 221438, "start": 2214.38, "end": 2219.3, "text": " Let me throw a real provocation at you, though. Because we live in a consumer-driven society.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 3507, 257, 957, 24568, 399, 412, 291, 11, 1673, 13, 1436, 321, 1621, 294, 257, 9711, 12, 25456, 4086, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 221438, "start": 2219.7400000000002, "end": 2221.88, "text": " What if the drummer just wants to hear more vocals?", "tokens": [50633, 708, 498, 264, 38535, 445, 2738, 281, 1568, 544, 28441, 30, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 221438, "start": 2222.1800000000003, "end": 2223.9, "text": " Oh, this happens all the time.", "tokens": [50755, 876, 11, 341, 2314, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 221438, "start": 2223.96, "end": 2227.52, "text": " Not because they need it for a musical cue, but simply because they like the sound of the", "tokens": [50844, 1726, 570, 436, 643, 309, 337, 257, 9165, 22656, 11, 457, 2935, 570, 436, 411, 264, 1626, 295, 264, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 221438, "start": 2227.52, "end": 2234.32, "text": " singer's voice. Shouldn't a personalized system give the user exactly what they prefer to consume?", "tokens": [51022, 11564, 311, 3177, 13, 34170, 380, 257, 28415, 1185, 976, 264, 4195, 2293, 437, 436, 4382, 281, 14732, 30, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 221438, "start": 2234.62, "end": 2236.94, "text": " Isn't that the definition of a good user experience?", "tokens": [51377, 6998, 380, 300, 264, 7123, 295, 257, 665, 4195, 1752, 30, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 221438, "start": 2237.1, "end": 2242.0, "text": " That is the ultimate temptation of the algorithmic age. But Flickshenand lays out what I consider", "tokens": [51501, 663, 307, 264, 9705, 30423, 295, 264, 9284, 299, 3205, 13, 583, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 474, 32714, 484, 437, 286, 1949, 51746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144916370511055, "compression_ratio": 1.6277602523659307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040558196624756e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 224200, "start": 2242.0, "end": 2244.6, "text": " the absolute golden rule of this entire essay.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 8236, 9729, 4978, 295, 341, 2302, 16238, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 224200, "start": 2244.76, "end": 2245.46, "text": " Okay. What is it?", "tokens": [50503, 1033, 13, 708, 307, 309, 30, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 224200, "start": 2245.46, "end": 2251.98, "text": " System designers must ask this specific question. Which projection of the shared state best preserves", "tokens": [50538, 8910, 16196, 1633, 1029, 341, 2685, 1168, 13, 3013, 22743, 295, 264, 5507, 1785, 1151, 1183, 9054, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 224200, "start": 2251.98, "end": 2254.56, "text": " this participant's next admissible continuation?", "tokens": [50864, 341, 24950, 311, 958, 5910, 41073, 29357, 30, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 224200, "start": 2254.98, "end": 2261.42, "text": " The next admissible continuation. That is such a heavy, dense phrase. What does that actually mean", "tokens": [51014, 440, 958, 5910, 41073, 29357, 13, 663, 307, 1270, 257, 4676, 11, 18011, 9535, 13, 708, 775, 300, 767, 914, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 224200, "start": 2261.42, "end": 2263.36, "text": " in practice? Unpack that for me.", "tokens": [51336, 294, 3124, 30, 1156, 9539, 300, 337, 385, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 224200, "start": 2263.48, "end": 2269.38, "text": " It means we have to stop optimizing systems for immediate, frictionless preference or enjoyment.", "tokens": [51439, 467, 1355, 321, 362, 281, 1590, 40425, 3652, 337, 11629, 11, 17710, 1832, 17502, 420, 32013, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 224200, "start": 2269.58, "end": 2269.8, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51744, 1033, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14780705829836288, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.694503153244764e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 226980, "start": 2269.8, "end": 2275.1600000000003, "text": " If you are the monitor engineer and you optimize only for what the drummer likes to hear, you", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 366, 264, 6002, 11403, 293, 291, 19719, 787, 337, 437, 264, 38535, 5902, 281, 1568, 11, 291, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 226980, "start": 2275.1600000000003, "end": 2280.36, "text": " crank the vocals. But by doing that, you raise the noise floor and drown out the bass line.", "tokens": [50633, 21263, 264, 28441, 13, 583, 538, 884, 300, 11, 291, 5300, 264, 5658, 4123, 293, 20337, 484, 264, 10136, 1622, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 226980, "start": 2280.44, "end": 2282.02, "text": " And the bass line is what they actually need.", "tokens": [50897, 400, 264, 10136, 1622, 307, 437, 436, 767, 643, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 226980, "start": 2282.1600000000003, "end": 2286.7000000000003, "text": " The bass line is the specific signal the drummer needs to perceive to keep the rhythm for the", "tokens": [50983, 440, 10136, 1622, 307, 264, 2685, 6358, 264, 38535, 2203, 281, 20281, 281, 1066, 264, 11801, 337, 264, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 226980, "start": 2286.7000000000003, "end": 2293.6000000000004, "text": " next 16 bars. Optimizing for immediate comfort, eventually, mathematically, optimizes away the", "tokens": [51210, 958, 3165, 10228, 13, 35013, 3319, 337, 11629, 3400, 11, 4728, 11, 44003, 11, 5028, 5660, 1314, 264, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 226980, "start": 2293.6000000000004, "end": 2297.6800000000003, "text": " very cues that keep a person capable of continuing their task in the shared world.", "tokens": [51555, 588, 32192, 300, 1066, 257, 954, 8189, 295, 9289, 641, 5633, 294, 264, 5507, 1002, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05795576243565, "compression_ratio": 1.7649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017325029127788e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 229768, "start": 2297.68, "end": 2302.56, "text": " That is profound. A healthy monitor is not a historical profile of your past desires.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 14382, 13, 316, 4627, 6002, 307, 406, 257, 8584, 7964, 295, 428, 1791, 18005, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135127498678964, "compression_ratio": 1.6994818652849741, "no_speech_prob": 2.044245848986659e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 229768, "start": 2303.04, "end": 2307.7599999999998, "text": " It is a dynamic control surface that equips you to successfully execute future actions.", "tokens": [50633, 467, 307, 257, 8546, 1969, 3753, 300, 1267, 2600, 291, 281, 10727, 14483, 2027, 5909, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135127498678964, "compression_ratio": 1.6994818652849741, "no_speech_prob": 2.044245848986659e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 229768, "start": 2307.9199999999996, "end": 2312.3999999999996, "text": " Exactly. A static profile traps you in a feedback loop of your past preferences.", "tokens": [50877, 7587, 13, 316, 13437, 7964, 24173, 291, 294, 257, 5824, 6367, 295, 428, 1791, 21910, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135127498678964, "compression_ratio": 1.6994818652849741, "no_speech_prob": 2.044245848986659e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 229768, "start": 2312.8199999999997, "end": 2316.3599999999997, "text": " A dynamic control surface equips you with the capacity for future action.", "tokens": [51122, 316, 8546, 1969, 3753, 1267, 2600, 291, 365, 264, 6042, 337, 2027, 3069, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135127498678964, "compression_ratio": 1.6994818652849741, "no_speech_prob": 2.044245848986659e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 231636, "start": 2316.36, "end": 2323.6400000000003, "text": " And a platform that only feeds you what you like is actively disabling your capacity to navigate the", "tokens": [50365, 400, 257, 3663, 300, 787, 23712, 291, 437, 291, 411, 307, 13022, 717, 20112, 428, 6042, 281, 12350, 264, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13578393242575906, "compression_ratio": 1.5683760683760684, "no_speech_prob": 1.694510525819537e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 231636, "start": 2323.6400000000003, "end": 2330.88, "text": " friction of the shared world. It is slowly blinding you to the signals you need to function as a citizen.", "tokens": [50729, 17710, 295, 264, 5507, 1002, 13, 467, 307, 5692, 6865, 278, 291, 281, 264, 12354, 291, 643, 281, 2445, 382, 257, 13326, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13578393242575906, "compression_ratio": 1.5683760683760684, "no_speech_prob": 1.694510525819537e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 231636, "start": 2331.1200000000003, "end": 2331.94, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51103, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13578393242575906, "compression_ratio": 1.5683760683760684, "no_speech_prob": 1.694510525819537e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 231636, "start": 2332.06, "end": 2334.52, "text": " Okay. This complex dynamic recovering system,", "tokens": [51150, 1033, 13, 639, 3997, 8546, 29180, 1185, 11, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13578393242575906, "compression_ratio": 1.5683760683760684, "no_speech_prob": 1.694510525819537e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 231636, "start": 2334.7200000000003, "end": 2340.96, "text": " the true hall of monitors, sounds incredible when it works. It's responsive. It's tailored. It keeps", "tokens": [51283, 264, 2074, 6500, 295, 26518, 11, 3263, 4651, 562, 309, 1985, 13, 467, 311, 21826, 13, 467, 311, 34858, 13, 467, 5965, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13578393242575906, "compression_ratio": 1.5683760683760684, "no_speech_prob": 1.694510525819537e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 234096, "start": 2340.96, "end": 2344.56, "text": " everyone coordinated without forcing them into identical realities.", "tokens": [50365, 1518, 29591, 1553, 19030, 552, 666, 14800, 27785, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803887008072495, "compression_ratio": 1.490909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617291310333515e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 234096, "start": 2344.64, "end": 2346.1, "text": " When it works, it's beautiful.", "tokens": [50549, 1133, 309, 1985, 11, 309, 311, 2238, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803887008072495, "compression_ratio": 1.490909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617291310333515e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 234096, "start": 2346.42, "end": 2352.06, "text": " But it begs a massive structural question. Who ensures it doesn't break down? Who audits the", "tokens": [50638, 583, 309, 4612, 82, 257, 5994, 15067, 1168, 13, 2102, 28111, 309, 1177, 380, 1821, 760, 30, 2102, 2379, 1208, 264, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803887008072495, "compression_ratio": 1.490909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617291310333515e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 234096, "start": 2352.06, "end": 2355.64, "text": " algorithm to make sure the monitor hasn't quietly mutated into a mirror?", "tokens": [50920, 9284, 281, 652, 988, 264, 6002, 6132, 380, 19141, 5839, 770, 666, 257, 8013, 30, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803887008072495, "compression_ratio": 1.490909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617291310333515e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 234096, "start": 2355.88, "end": 2359.2400000000002, "text": " This is what Fliction terms the crisis of ambient verification.", "tokens": [51111, 639, 307, 437, 3235, 4105, 2115, 264, 5869, 295, 22997, 30206, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803887008072495, "compression_ratio": 1.490909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617291310333515e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 235924, "start": 2359.24, "end": 2364.2799999999997, "text": " The crisis of ambient verification. The essay points out the ultimate cheat code of the", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5869, 295, 22997, 30206, 13, 440, 16238, 2793, 484, 264, 9705, 17470, 3089, 295, 264, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 235924, "start": 2364.2799999999997, "end": 2367.4199999999996, "text": " Ross Band metaphor, right? The physical room itself. The air.", "tokens": [50617, 16140, 15462, 19157, 11, 558, 30, 440, 4001, 1808, 2564, 13, 440, 1988, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 235924, "start": 2367.4799999999996, "end": 2368.24, "text": " The air is free.", "tokens": [50777, 440, 1988, 307, 1737, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 235924, "start": 2368.3799999999997, "end": 2373.56, "text": " The acoustic environment provides free ambient verification. If the monitor mix goes completely", "tokens": [50822, 440, 26753, 2823, 6417, 1737, 22997, 30206, 13, 759, 264, 6002, 2890, 1709, 2584, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 235924, "start": 2373.56, "end": 2378.68, "text": " haywire, anyone, the sound tech, the bass player, a fan in the front row, can simply pull their", "tokens": [51081, 4842, 42689, 11, 2878, 11, 264, 1626, 7553, 11, 264, 10136, 4256, 11, 257, 3429, 294, 264, 1868, 5386, 11, 393, 2935, 2235, 641, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 235924, "start": 2378.68, "end": 2383.16, "text": " earpiece out, listen to the open air, and check the shared state against what the musicians are doing.", "tokens": [51337, 1273, 15281, 484, 11, 2140, 281, 264, 1269, 1988, 11, 293, 1520, 264, 5507, 1785, 1970, 437, 264, 16916, 366, 884, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 235924, "start": 2383.8199999999997, "end": 2388.8199999999997, "text": " Exactly. The objective truth is literally vibrating the air molecules in the room. You can't fake it.", "tokens": [51594, 7587, 13, 440, 10024, 3494, 307, 3736, 47748, 264, 1988, 13093, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 509, 393, 380, 7592, 309, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08065160358225117, "compression_ratio": 1.68562874251497, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818525786483e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 238924, "start": 2389.24, "end": 2394.2999999999997, "text": " But if we connect this to the bigger picture of modern society, this is where the hammer drops.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 295, 4363, 4086, 11, 341, 307, 689, 264, 13017, 11438, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 238924, "start": 2394.4599999999996, "end": 2395.2, "text": " It drops hard.", "tokens": [50626, 467, 11438, 1152, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 238924, "start": 2395.3399999999997, "end": 2401.64, "text": " Distributed software, personalized social media feeds, massive algorithmic tech platforms.", "tokens": [50670, 9840, 2024, 4866, 4722, 11, 28415, 2093, 3021, 23712, 11, 5994, 9284, 299, 7553, 9473, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 238924, "start": 2402.3399999999997, "end": 2403.8399999999997, "text": " They have no room air.", "tokens": [51020, 814, 362, 572, 1808, 1988, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 238924, "start": 2404.0, "end": 2407.9399999999996, "text": " None. There is no ambient acoustic environment you can casually listen to.", "tokens": [51103, 14492, 13, 821, 307, 572, 22997, 26753, 2823, 291, 393, 34872, 2140, 281, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 238924, "start": 2408.16, "end": 2412.7, "text": " You cannot casually look past your own algorithmic feed to see the true state of the network.", "tokens": [51311, 509, 2644, 34872, 574, 1791, 428, 1065, 9284, 299, 3154, 281, 536, 264, 2074, 1785, 295, 264, 3209, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 238924, "start": 2412.8199999999997, "end": 2415.04, "text": " The network only exists through the interface.", "tokens": [51544, 440, 3209, 787, 8198, 807, 264, 9226, 13, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 238924, "start": 2415.18, "end": 2415.4399999999996, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51662, 1079, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 238924, "start": 2415.64, "end": 2418.74, "text": " That is the sharpest, most chilling warning in the text.", "tokens": [51685, 663, 307, 264, 8199, 377, 11, 881, 31047, 9164, 294, 264, 2487, 13, 51840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14955419745327028, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198916785917003e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 241924, "start": 2419.24, "end": 2422.3399999999997, "text": " A hall of mirrors doesn't trigger a system failure alarm.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 6500, 295, 24238, 1177, 380, 7875, 257, 1185, 7763, 14183, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 241924, "start": 2422.8599999999997, "end": 2425.4199999999996, "text": " The platform doesn't flash red when it traps you.", "tokens": [50546, 440, 3663, 1177, 380, 7319, 2182, 562, 309, 24173, 291, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 241924, "start": 2425.4199999999996, "end": 2431.2799999999997, "text": " It just quietly, efficiently keeps amplifying what is already loud and easy to justify the", "tokens": [50674, 467, 445, 19141, 11, 19621, 5965, 9731, 5489, 437, 307, 1217, 6588, 293, 1858, 281, 20833, 264, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 241924, "start": 2431.2799999999997, "end": 2435.72, "text": " things you already click on, the opinions you already hold, the outrage you already feel.", "tokens": [50967, 721, 291, 1217, 2052, 322, 11, 264, 11819, 291, 1217, 1797, 11, 264, 25933, 291, 1217, 841, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 241924, "start": 2435.7999999999997, "end": 2440.9199999999996, "text": " Meanwhile, the quiet, crucial, complex signals that you actually need to understand the nuances", "tokens": [51193, 13879, 11, 264, 5677, 11, 11462, 11, 3997, 12354, 300, 291, 767, 643, 281, 1223, 264, 38775, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 241924, "start": 2440.9199999999996, "end": 2443.2999999999997, "text": " of the world never cross your noise floor.", "tokens": [51449, 295, 264, 1002, 1128, 3278, 428, 5658, 4123, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10033519900574976, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 2.838069406221888e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 244330, "start": 2443.3, "end": 2443.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 244330, "start": 2444.36, "end": 2446.7200000000003, "text": " They aren't explicitly censored by a dictator.", "tokens": [50418, 814, 3212, 380, 20803, 19019, 2769, 538, 257, 42852, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 244330, "start": 2446.9, "end": 2450.26, "text": " They just never get amplified enough by the algorithm for you to perceive them.", "tokens": [50545, 814, 445, 1128, 483, 49237, 1547, 538, 264, 9284, 337, 291, 281, 20281, 552, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 244330, "start": 2450.52, "end": 2452.0600000000004, "text": " They're drowned out by your own preferences.", "tokens": [50726, 814, 434, 38233, 484, 538, 428, 1065, 21910, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 244330, "start": 2452.54, "end": 2455.2400000000002, "text": " And this brings us all the way back to the beginning of our conversation.", "tokens": [50827, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 264, 2863, 295, 527, 3761, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 244330, "start": 2455.7200000000003, "end": 2458.7400000000002, "text": " The return of the dark fourth sense of the word monitor.", "tokens": [50986, 440, 2736, 295, 264, 2877, 6409, 2020, 295, 264, 1349, 6002, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 244330, "start": 2458.96, "end": 2459.42, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51148, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 244330, "start": 2459.6400000000003, "end": 2459.8, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51182, 865, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16889385793400907, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 1.748291724064377e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 245980, "start": 2459.8, "end": 2464.3, "text": " Without that ambient verification, without the room air to check reality against the", "tokens": [50365, 9129, 300, 22997, 30206, 11, 1553, 264, 1808, 1988, 281, 1520, 4103, 1970, 264, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 245980, "start": 2464.3, "end": 2468.82, "text": " system, degrades entirely into its purely supervisory function.", "tokens": [50590, 1185, 11, 368, 22626, 7696, 666, 1080, 17491, 34409, 827, 2445, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 245980, "start": 2468.92, "end": 2469.84, "text": " It watches us.", "tokens": [50821, 467, 17062, 505, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 245980, "start": 2470.1800000000003, "end": 2473.5, "text": " It mines our behavioral data to optimize for engagement.", "tokens": [50884, 467, 25398, 527, 19124, 1412, 281, 19719, 337, 8742, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 245980, "start": 2473.7000000000003, "end": 2477.4, "text": " It checks us for gross rule violations or terms of service breaches.", "tokens": [51060, 467, 13834, 505, 337, 11367, 4978, 30405, 420, 2115, 295, 2643, 1403, 13272, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 245980, "start": 2477.6600000000003, "end": 2480.7000000000003, "text": " But it does absolutely nothing to expand what we can perceive.", "tokens": [51258, 583, 309, 775, 3122, 1825, 281, 5268, 437, 321, 393, 20281, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 245980, "start": 2481.0, "end": 2485.1600000000003, "text": " And it does absolutely nothing to help us coordinate with our fellow citizens who are trapped in their", "tokens": [51425, 400, 309, 775, 3122, 1825, 281, 854, 505, 15670, 365, 527, 7177, 7180, 567, 366, 14994, 294, 641, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1427691650390625, "compression_ratio": 1.691449814126394, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362148181486846e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 248516, "start": 2485.16, "end": 2486.12, "text": " own distinct mirrors.", "tokens": [50365, 1065, 10644, 24238, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 248516, "start": 2486.46, "end": 2490.2599999999998, "text": " It stops being a tool for us to use and it becomes a tool operating on us.", "tokens": [50430, 467, 10094, 885, 257, 2290, 337, 505, 281, 764, 293, 309, 3643, 257, 2290, 7447, 322, 505, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 248516, "start": 2490.46, "end": 2490.7999999999997, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50630, 48746, 736, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 248516, "start": 2491.08, "end": 2495.8399999999997, "text": " It is the hall monitor checking our hall pass while we have no idea what building we are even in.", "tokens": [50661, 467, 307, 264, 6500, 6002, 8568, 527, 6500, 1320, 1339, 321, 362, 572, 1558, 437, 2390, 321, 366, 754, 294, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 248516, "start": 2496.08, "end": 2496.2799999999997, "text": " Man.", "tokens": [50911, 2458, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 248516, "start": 2497.2599999999998, "end": 2504.24, "text": " So to prove this isn't just an extended hyper-specific audio metaphor, Flickshinen rapidly applies this", "tokens": [50970, 407, 281, 7081, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 364, 10913, 9848, 12, 29258, 6278, 19157, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 5636, 12910, 13165, 341, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 248516, "start": 2504.24, "end": 2509.3199999999997, "text": " architecture to several real-world, high-stakes environments in the final sections of the essay.", "tokens": [51319, 9482, 281, 2940, 957, 12, 13217, 11, 1090, 12, 372, 3419, 12388, 294, 264, 2572, 10863, 295, 264, 16238, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 248516, "start": 2509.64, "end": 2511.2999999999997, "text": " It scales really well.", "tokens": [51589, 467, 17408, 534, 731, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807162023223607, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813625566633686e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 251130, "start": 2511.3, "end": 2515.48, "text": " I want us to really dig into these examples because it scales the theory beautifully and", "tokens": [50365, 286, 528, 505, 281, 534, 2528, 666, 613, 5110, 570, 309, 17408, 264, 5261, 16525, 293, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 251130, "start": 2515.48, "end": 2517.6600000000003, "text": " shows how universal these mechanics are.", "tokens": [50574, 3110, 577, 11455, 613, 12939, 366, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 251130, "start": 2517.8, "end": 2518.86, "text": " Let's start with laboratories.", "tokens": [50690, 961, 311, 722, 365, 41013, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 251130, "start": 2519.36, "end": 2519.5800000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50768, 1779, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 251130, "start": 2519.78, "end": 2524.7200000000003, "text": " Think about a massive multi-million dollar particle physics lab.", "tokens": [50789, 6557, 466, 257, 5994, 4825, 12, 40388, 7241, 12359, 10649, 2715, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 251130, "start": 2524.94, "end": 2529.84, "text": " You have the principal investigator, the PI, who is looking at data visualizations, trying", "tokens": [51047, 509, 362, 264, 9716, 38330, 11, 264, 27176, 11, 567, 307, 1237, 412, 1412, 5056, 14455, 11, 1382, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 251130, "start": 2529.84, "end": 2534.4, "text": " to find broad statistical patterns across months of experimental data.", "tokens": [51292, 281, 915, 4152, 22820, 8294, 2108, 2493, 295, 17069, 1412, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 251130, "start": 2534.5800000000004, "end": 2534.78, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51529, 4894, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 251130, "start": 2534.98, "end": 2540.38, "text": " And sitting right next to them, you have the lab technician who is looking at a live, raw telemetry", "tokens": [51549, 400, 3798, 558, 958, 281, 552, 11, 291, 362, 264, 2715, 38247, 567, 307, 1237, 412, 257, 1621, 11, 8936, 4304, 5537, 627, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1283175558106512, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.6351777787707023e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 254038, "start": 2540.38, "end": 2545.94, "text": " feed of the physical instrument, watching for a very specific voltage spike that indicates", "tokens": [50365, 3154, 295, 264, 4001, 7198, 11, 1976, 337, 257, 588, 2685, 8352, 21053, 300, 16203, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 254038, "start": 2545.94, "end": 2547.52, "text": " a hardware failure right now.", "tokens": [50643, 257, 8837, 7763, 558, 586, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 254038, "start": 2547.6600000000003, "end": 2549.1800000000003, "text": " They require totally different views.", "tokens": [50729, 814, 3651, 3879, 819, 6809, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 254038, "start": 2549.52, "end": 2550.38, "text": " Radically different.", "tokens": [50822, 9654, 984, 819, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 254038, "start": 2550.38, "end": 2555.32, "text": " The PI needs a heavily smoothed, time-averaged macro projection.", "tokens": [50865, 440, 27176, 2203, 257, 10950, 5508, 292, 11, 565, 12, 20655, 2980, 18887, 22743, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 254038, "start": 2555.84, "end": 2559.2000000000003, "text": " The tech needs a high-frequency, raw micro projection.", "tokens": [51138, 440, 7553, 2203, 257, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 11, 8936, 4532, 22743, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 254038, "start": 2559.42, "end": 2564.44, "text": " But, and this is the crucial part, both of those wildly different views would be strict", "tokens": [51317, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 11462, 644, 11, 1293, 295, 729, 34731, 819, 6809, 576, 312, 10910, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 254038, "start": 2564.44, "end": 2568.58, "text": " mathematical projections of the exact same underlying experimental data.", "tokens": [51568, 18894, 32371, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 14217, 17069, 1412, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313436054048084, "compression_ratio": 1.684981684981685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102629212672026e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 256858, "start": 2568.58, "end": 2573.9, "text": " If the PI software starts aliasing the data to make it look cleaner, the experiment is", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 27176, 4722, 3719, 10198, 3349, 264, 1412, 281, 652, 309, 574, 16532, 11, 264, 5120, 307, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 256858, "start": 2573.9, "end": 2574.3199999999997, "text": " invalid.", "tokens": [50631, 34702, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 256858, "start": 2574.64, "end": 2579.72, "text": " Then you move into even higher stakes, cockpits, and hospital operating rooms.", "tokens": [50668, 1396, 291, 1286, 666, 754, 2946, 28429, 11, 11241, 79, 1208, 11, 293, 4530, 7447, 9396, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 256858, "start": 2580.22, "end": 2585.56, "text": " You have incredibly complex checklists and role-specific digital displays.", "tokens": [50947, 509, 362, 6252, 3997, 1520, 36693, 293, 3090, 12, 29258, 4562, 20119, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 256858, "start": 2585.7, "end": 2586.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51221, 1779, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 256858, "start": 2586.18, "end": 2591.22, "text": " The pilot flying the plane needs different instrumentation than the co-pilot handling communications.", "tokens": [51245, 440, 9691, 7137, 264, 5720, 2203, 819, 7198, 399, 813, 264, 598, 12, 79, 31516, 13175, 15163, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 256858, "start": 2591.64, "end": 2596.24, "text": " The lead surgeon needs a different beta stream than the anesthesiologist monitoring vitals.", "tokens": [51518, 440, 1477, 22913, 2203, 257, 819, 9861, 4309, 813, 264, 31750, 8076, 72, 9201, 11028, 9467, 1124, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16807952293982872, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 259624, "start": 2596.24, "end": 2600.7799999999997, "text": " And here I have to bring in footnote 6, which references Thomas Sheridan's foundational", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 286, 362, 281, 1565, 294, 2671, 22178, 1386, 11, 597, 15400, 8500, 11789, 31675, 311, 32195, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 259624, "start": 2600.7799999999997, "end": 2602.06, "text": " work on telerobotics.", "tokens": [50592, 589, 322, 256, 6185, 996, 42131, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 259624, "start": 2602.22, "end": 2602.8999999999996, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50664, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 259624, "start": 2603.5, "end": 2609.2999999999997, "text": " When you are flying a drone remotely or performing robotic surgery across a network, the cost of", "tokens": [50728, 1133, 291, 366, 7137, 257, 13852, 20824, 420, 10205, 30468, 7930, 2108, 257, 3209, 11, 264, 2063, 295, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 259624, "start": 2609.2999999999997, "end": 2614.3399999999997, "text": " a hall of monitors collapsing into a hall of mirrors isn't just a bad drum fill or someone", "tokens": [51018, 257, 6500, 295, 26518, 45339, 666, 257, 6500, 295, 24238, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 1578, 10206, 2836, 420, 1580, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 259624, "start": 2614.3399999999997, "end": 2615.3599999999997, "text": " getting mad on the internet.", "tokens": [51270, 1242, 5244, 322, 264, 4705, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 259624, "start": 2615.4799999999996, "end": 2617.4799999999996, "text": " It is actual, immediate physical harm.", "tokens": [51327, 467, 307, 3539, 11, 11629, 4001, 6491, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 259624, "start": 2617.62, "end": 2617.8999999999996, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51434, 1079, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1170803165435791, "compression_ratio": 1.5179282868525896, "no_speech_prob": 2.236422201942756e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 261790, "start": 2617.9, "end": 2623.62, "text": " If the surgeon's haptic feedback monitor aliases the soft tissue resistance to feel like empty", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 22913, 311, 324, 32307, 5824, 6002, 10198, 1957, 264, 2787, 12404, 7335, 281, 841, 411, 6707, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 261790, "start": 2623.62, "end": 2625.08, "text": " space, they cut an artery.", "tokens": [50651, 1901, 11, 436, 1723, 364, 38520, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 261790, "start": 2625.62, "end": 2628.1800000000003, "text": " The architecture of these systems has to be bulletproof.", "tokens": [50751, 440, 9482, 295, 613, 3652, 575, 281, 312, 11632, 15690, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 261790, "start": 2628.7200000000003, "end": 2631.58, "text": " The recoverability of the shared state must be instantaneous.", "tokens": [50906, 440, 8114, 2310, 295, 264, 5507, 1785, 1633, 312, 45596, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 261790, "start": 2632.1800000000003, "end": 2635.54, "text": " How does this apply to something less mechanical like education?", "tokens": [51079, 1012, 775, 341, 3079, 281, 746, 1570, 12070, 411, 3309, 30, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 261790, "start": 2635.7400000000002, "end": 2636.5, "text": " What about classrooms?", "tokens": [51257, 708, 466, 22890, 30, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14829266698736893, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.981367977674231e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 263650, "start": 2636.5, "end": 2641.42, "text": " A classroom, at its absolute best, is a perfectly functioning hall of monitors.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 7419, 11, 412, 1080, 8236, 1151, 11, 307, 257, 6239, 18483, 6500, 295, 26518, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 263650, "start": 2641.6, "end": 2643.8, "text": " You have 30 distinct students.", "tokens": [50620, 509, 362, 2217, 10644, 1731, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 263650, "start": 2644.68, "end": 2648.14, "text": " Different students might need different pacing, different analogies, or different scaffolding", "tokens": [50774, 20825, 1731, 1062, 643, 819, 43285, 11, 819, 16660, 530, 11, 420, 819, 44094, 278, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 263650, "start": 2648.14, "end": 2650.4, "text": " to learn a complex mathematical concept.", "tokens": [50947, 281, 1466, 257, 3997, 18894, 3410, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 263650, "start": 2650.52, "end": 2653.48, "text": " A good teacher provides 30 different projections of the lesson.", "tokens": [51066, 316, 665, 5027, 6417, 2217, 819, 32371, 295, 264, 6898, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 263650, "start": 2653.6, "end": 2659.6, "text": " But all 30 projections must be rigorously answerable to the same underlying curriculum, the shared", "tokens": [51220, 583, 439, 2217, 32371, 1633, 312, 42191, 5098, 1867, 712, 281, 264, 912, 14217, 14302, 11, 264, 5507, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 263650, "start": 2659.6, "end": 2660.02, "text": " state.", "tokens": [51520, 1785, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13066800086052863, "compression_ratio": 1.640316205533597, "no_speech_prob": 2.2103484407370866e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 266002, "start": 2660.02, "end": 2665.74, "text": " If a school system decides to isolate struggling students onto entirely different, dumbed-down", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1395, 1185, 14898, 281, 25660, 9314, 1731, 3911, 7696, 819, 11, 10316, 292, 12, 5093, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 266002, "start": 2665.74, "end": 2669.68, "text": " tracks that can't be checked against the shared standard of the main curriculum, they haven't", "tokens": [50651, 10218, 300, 393, 380, 312, 10033, 1970, 264, 5507, 3832, 295, 264, 2135, 14302, 11, 436, 2378, 380, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 266002, "start": 2669.68, "end": 2670.78, "text": " personalized education.", "tokens": [50848, 28415, 3309, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 266002, "start": 2671.32, "end": 2672.96, "text": " They have built a hall of mirrors.", "tokens": [50930, 814, 362, 3094, 257, 6500, 295, 24238, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 266002, "start": 2673.14, "end": 2677.02, "text": " They have trapped those students in an unrecoverable reality.", "tokens": [51021, 814, 362, 14994, 729, 1731, 294, 364, 20584, 12516, 712, 4103, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 266002, "start": 2677.2599999999998, "end": 2677.7599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51227, 7587, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 266002, "start": 2678.42, "end": 2681.74, "text": " Finally, Flickshon points to the sharpest test of all.", "tokens": [51285, 6288, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 266, 2793, 281, 264, 8199, 377, 1500, 295, 439, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 266002, "start": 2682.5, "end": 2689.8, "text": " Multi-agent systems, autonomous drone swarms, complex AI networks, distributed computing grids.", "tokens": [51489, 29238, 12, 559, 317, 3652, 11, 23797, 13852, 1693, 19537, 11, 3997, 7318, 9590, 11, 12631, 15866, 677, 3742, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14721627362006534, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047229935121758e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 268980, "start": 2689.8, "end": 2693.1000000000004, "text": " This is where the theory becomes vital for the future of technology.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 264, 5261, 3643, 11707, 337, 264, 2027, 295, 2899, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 268980, "start": 2693.7200000000003, "end": 2698.8, "text": " In a true multi-agent system, no single component ever holds the complete state of the system", "tokens": [50561, 682, 257, 2074, 4825, 12, 559, 317, 1185, 11, 572, 2167, 6542, 1562, 9190, 264, 3566, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 268980, "start": 2698.8, "end": 2700.1000000000004, "text": " in its memory at once.", "tokens": [50815, 294, 1080, 4675, 412, 1564, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 268980, "start": 2700.2400000000002, "end": 2701.6200000000003, "text": " It's computationally impossible.", "tokens": [50887, 467, 311, 24903, 379, 6243, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 268980, "start": 2701.76, "end": 2705.7400000000002, "text": " Wait, so there is no master brain sitting in the center that sees everything perfectly.", "tokens": [50963, 3802, 11, 370, 456, 307, 572, 4505, 3567, 3798, 294, 264, 3056, 300, 8194, 1203, 6239, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 268980, "start": 2706.1600000000003, "end": 2706.7200000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51183, 7587, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 268980, "start": 2707.3, "end": 2715.02, "text": " And Footnote 7 brings in Edwin Hutchins' incredible 1995 cognitive science study on U.S. Navy ship", "tokens": [51240, 400, 20989, 22178, 1614, 5607, 294, 3977, 9136, 48499, 1292, 6, 4651, 22601, 15605, 3497, 2979, 322, 624, 13, 50, 13, 15659, 5374, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 268980, "start": 2715.02, "end": 2716.2200000000003, "text": " navigation teams.", "tokens": [51626, 17346, 5491, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 268980, "start": 2716.44, "end": 2717.1800000000003, "text": " Navy ships.", "tokens": [51697, 15659, 11434, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13721610381539945, "compression_ratio": 1.5470383275261324, "no_speech_prob": 2.060286620128582e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 271718, "start": 2717.18, "end": 2722.24, "text": " Yeah, Hutchins lived on these massive ships and observed that the navigating mine of the", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 48499, 1292, 5152, 322, 613, 5994, 11434, 293, 13095, 300, 264, 32054, 3892, 295, 264, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 271718, "start": 2722.24, "end": 2723.8799999999997, "text": " vessel does not belong to the captain.", "tokens": [50618, 18098, 775, 406, 5784, 281, 264, 14871, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 271718, "start": 2724.06, "end": 2725.62, "text": " It doesn't belong to the head navigator.", "tokens": [50709, 467, 1177, 380, 5784, 281, 264, 1378, 7407, 1639, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 271718, "start": 2725.8199999999997, "end": 2726.74, "text": " Who does it belong to?", "tokens": [50797, 2102, 775, 309, 5784, 281, 30, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 271718, "start": 2727.08, "end": 2732.8799999999997, "text": " The cognitive mine is the entire sociotechnical assembly, the quartermasters taking physical", "tokens": [50860, 440, 15605, 3892, 307, 264, 2302, 3075, 31843, 804, 12103, 11, 264, 6555, 3799, 1559, 1940, 4001, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 271718, "start": 2732.8799999999997, "end": 2738.54, "text": " bearings, the radar operators looking at screens, the officers charting the map, the communication", "tokens": [51150, 36297, 11, 264, 16544, 19077, 1237, 412, 11171, 11, 264, 9199, 6927, 278, 264, 4471, 11, 264, 6101, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 271718, "start": 2738.54, "end": 2739.7, "text": " protocols they use.", "tokens": [51433, 20618, 436, 764, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 271718, "start": 2739.96, "end": 2743.24, "text": " They're all sharing partial, highly specific views.", "tokens": [51504, 814, 434, 439, 5414, 14641, 11, 5405, 2685, 6809, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515546728063512, "compression_ratio": 1.6977611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047303660869487e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 274324, "start": 2743.24, "end": 2743.72, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 274324, "start": 2744.2, "end": 2748.3999999999996, "text": " The true shared state, the exact position of the ship in the ocean, is never directly", "tokens": [50413, 440, 2074, 5507, 1785, 11, 264, 1900, 2535, 295, 264, 5374, 294, 264, 7810, 11, 307, 1128, 3838, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 274324, "start": 2748.3999999999996, "end": 2750.16, "text": " observable by any one person.", "tokens": [50623, 9951, 712, 538, 604, 472, 954, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 274324, "start": 2750.2799999999997, "end": 2750.8199999999997, "text": " That's wild.", "tokens": [50717, 663, 311, 4868, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 274324, "start": 2750.9599999999996, "end": 2755.66, "text": " Therefore, the rigorous discipline of preserving recoverable projections isn't just a nice", "tokens": [50751, 7504, 11, 264, 29882, 13635, 295, 33173, 8114, 712, 32371, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 1481, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 274324, "start": 2755.66, "end": 2756.5, "text": " feature for the crew.", "tokens": [50986, 4111, 337, 264, 7260, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 274324, "start": 2756.8399999999997, "end": 2760.72, "text": " It is the entire cognitive basis that prevents the ship from crashing into a reef.", "tokens": [51045, 467, 307, 264, 2302, 15605, 5143, 300, 22367, 264, 5374, 490, 26900, 666, 257, 25345, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 274324, "start": 2760.8599999999997, "end": 2763.02, "text": " So the rock band was never just a clever metaphor.", "tokens": [51246, 407, 264, 3727, 4116, 390, 1128, 445, 257, 13494, 19157, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 274324, "start": 2763.4599999999996, "end": 2768.52, "text": " It is just the clearest, most intuitive, visceral instance of a universal physical requirement", "tokens": [51376, 467, 307, 445, 264, 1233, 17363, 11, 881, 21769, 11, 1452, 47879, 5197, 295, 257, 11455, 4001, 11695, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09773614488798997, "compression_ratio": 1.6843971631205674, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451519809951748e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 276852, "start": 2768.52, "end": 2772.84, "text": " for any group of agents trying to do something complex together in a noisy world.", "tokens": [50365, 337, 604, 1594, 295, 12554, 1382, 281, 360, 746, 3997, 1214, 294, 257, 24518, 1002, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 276852, "start": 2773.2, "end": 2773.7599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50599, 7587, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 276852, "start": 2774.16, "end": 2777.08, "text": " It is the blueprint for survival in a complex environment.", "tokens": [50647, 467, 307, 264, 35868, 337, 12559, 294, 257, 3997, 2823, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 276852, "start": 2777.4, "end": 2782.96, "text": " We have covered a massive amount of conceptual ground today, from psychoacoustics and signal", "tokens": [50809, 492, 362, 5343, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 24106, 2727, 965, 11, 490, 33355, 326, 15849, 1167, 293, 6358, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 276852, "start": 2782.96, "end": 2788.6, "text": " detection theory to the architecture of social media and the navigation of Navy ships.", "tokens": [51087, 17784, 5261, 281, 264, 9482, 295, 2093, 3021, 293, 264, 17346, 295, 15659, 11434, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 276852, "start": 2788.7599999999998, "end": 2789.54, "text": " We really have.", "tokens": [51377, 492, 534, 362, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 276852, "start": 2789.66, "end": 2793.74, "text": " But if I had to pull it all together based on Fliction's text, it is this.", "tokens": [51422, 583, 498, 286, 632, 281, 2235, 309, 439, 1214, 2361, 322, 3235, 4105, 311, 2487, 11, 309, 307, 341, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 276852, "start": 2794.56, "end": 2797.5, "text": " A common world does not require a common mix.", "tokens": [51667, 316, 2689, 1002, 775, 406, 3651, 257, 2689, 2890, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12456698166696649, "compression_ratio": 1.6013745704467355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810581126933346e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 279750, "start": 2797.5, "end": 2798.46, "text": " No, it doesn't.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 279750, "start": 2798.6, "end": 2803.8, "text": " We do not all need to see the exact same feed, read the exact same articles, or hold the", "tokens": [50420, 492, 360, 406, 439, 643, 281, 536, 264, 1900, 912, 3154, 11, 1401, 264, 1900, 912, 11290, 11, 420, 1797, 264, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 279750, "start": 2803.8, "end": 2808.34, "text": " exact same perspectives to be a highly functioning, coordinated society.", "tokens": [50680, 1900, 912, 16766, 281, 312, 257, 5405, 18483, 11, 29591, 4086, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 279750, "start": 2808.78, "end": 2812.76, "text": " Differences in perception are actually required for a complex system to operate.", "tokens": [50929, 413, 12612, 2667, 294, 12860, 366, 767, 4739, 337, 257, 3997, 1185, 281, 9651, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 279750, "start": 2813.02, "end": 2818.54, "text": " But, and this is the massive but, it absolutely requires that every individual mix remains", "tokens": [51141, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 5994, 457, 11, 309, 3122, 7029, 300, 633, 2609, 2890, 7023, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 279750, "start": 2818.54, "end": 2820.62, "text": " a verifiable mix of something common.", "tokens": [51417, 257, 1306, 30876, 2890, 295, 746, 2689, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 279750, "start": 2820.88, "end": 2823.72, "text": " We have to be able to find our way back to the shared reality.", "tokens": [51534, 492, 362, 281, 312, 1075, 281, 915, 527, 636, 646, 281, 264, 5507, 4103, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 279750, "start": 2823.94, "end": 2825.5, "text": " We have to be able to listen to the room.", "tokens": [51687, 492, 362, 281, 312, 1075, 281, 2140, 281, 264, 1808, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07733930417192661, "compression_ratio": 1.7508896797153024, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798822753515518e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 282550, "start": 2825.5, "end": 2829.92, "text": " I want to challenge everyone listening right now to apply this directly to your own life.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 528, 281, 3430, 1518, 4764, 558, 586, 281, 3079, 341, 3838, 281, 428, 1065, 993, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 282550, "start": 2830.08, "end": 2833.96, "text": " Yeah, take a hard look at the enterprise software you were forced to use for work every day.", "tokens": [50594, 865, 11, 747, 257, 1152, 574, 412, 264, 14132, 4722, 291, 645, 7579, 281, 764, 337, 589, 633, 786, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 282550, "start": 2834.6, "end": 2838.06, "text": " Look closely at the algorithmic feeds you scroll through on your phone tonight.", "tokens": [50820, 2053, 8185, 412, 264, 9284, 299, 23712, 291, 11369, 807, 322, 428, 2593, 4440, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 282550, "start": 2838.46, "end": 2842.58, "text": " Ask yourself, are you standing in a hall of monitors where you can still look through the", "tokens": [51013, 12320, 1803, 11, 366, 291, 4877, 294, 257, 6500, 295, 26518, 689, 291, 393, 920, 574, 807, 264, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 282550, "start": 2842.58, "end": 2844.64, "text": " interface and verify the real world?", "tokens": [51219, 9226, 293, 16888, 264, 957, 1002, 30, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 282550, "start": 2845.36, "end": 2851.46, "text": " Or have the windows been quietly, comfortably replaced by mirrors, reflecting nothing but your", "tokens": [51358, 1610, 362, 264, 9309, 668, 19141, 11, 25101, 10772, 538, 24238, 11, 23543, 1825, 457, 428, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10751699287200643, "compression_ratio": 1.6406779661016948, "no_speech_prob": 2.101104229837447e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 285146, "start": 2851.46, "end": 2853.54, "text": " own past choices back at you?", "tokens": [50365, 1065, 1791, 7994, 646, 412, 291, 30, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 285146, "start": 2853.54, "end": 2856.36, "text": " It is a genuinely haunting question.", "tokens": [50469, 467, 307, 257, 17839, 44512, 1168, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 285146, "start": 2857.04, "end": 2861.88, "text": " And I want to leave you with one final provocative thought to mull over as you go about your day.", "tokens": [50644, 400, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 472, 2572, 47663, 1194, 281, 275, 858, 670, 382, 291, 352, 466, 428, 786, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 285146, "start": 2861.92, "end": 2862.42, "text": " That is it.", "tokens": [50888, 663, 307, 309, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 285146, "start": 2862.7, "end": 2868.78, "text": " If our modern digital lives are increasingly built on static profiles rather than dynamic", "tokens": [50927, 759, 527, 4363, 4562, 2909, 366, 12980, 3094, 322, 13437, 23693, 2831, 813, 8546, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 285146, "start": 2868.78, "end": 2874.68, "text": " control surfaces, and if there is no longer any digital room air to verify our shared state,", "tokens": [51231, 1969, 16130, 11, 293, 498, 456, 307, 572, 2854, 604, 4562, 1808, 1988, 281, 16888, 527, 5507, 1785, 11, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16495027213261046, "compression_ratio": 1.5541125541125542, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453785792492242e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 287468, "start": 2874.68, "end": 2880.66, "text": " how much of our current societal polarization, how much of our political rage, is actually just a", "tokens": [50365, 577, 709, 295, 527, 2190, 33472, 37736, 11, 577, 709, 295, 527, 3905, 20133, 11, 307, 767, 445, 257, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 287468, "start": 2880.66, "end": 2883.7599999999998, "text": " catastrophic architectural failure of perception scheduling?", "tokens": [50664, 34915, 26621, 7763, 295, 12860, 29055, 30, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 287468, "start": 2884.1, "end": 2884.48, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50836, 3153, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 287468, "start": 2884.48, "end": 2888.5, "text": " We think we're angry at each other, but what if our monitors are just aliasing the truth?", "tokens": [50855, 492, 519, 321, 434, 6884, 412, 1184, 661, 11, 457, 437, 498, 527, 26518, 366, 445, 10198, 3349, 264, 3494, 30, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 287468, "start": 2889.16, "end": 2891.3199999999997, "text": " What would a social network actually look like?", "tokens": [51089, 708, 576, 257, 2093, 3209, 767, 574, 411, 30, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 287468, "start": 2891.3799999999997, "end": 2895.3999999999996, "text": " How would it function if it were built by a live sound engineer trying to coordinate a band", "tokens": [51200, 1012, 576, 309, 2445, 498, 309, 645, 3094, 538, 257, 1621, 1626, 11403, 1382, 281, 15670, 257, 4116, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 287468, "start": 2895.3999999999996, "end": 2898.68, "text": " instead of an engagement algorithm trying to maximize watch time?", "tokens": [51401, 2602, 295, 364, 8742, 9284, 1382, 281, 19874, 1159, 565, 30, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 287468, "start": 2898.7999999999997, "end": 2899.58, "text": " That's a great thought.", "tokens": [51571, 663, 311, 257, 869, 1194, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149473001291086, "compression_ratio": 1.6317567567567568, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884403609470963e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 289958, "start": 2899.58, "end": 2904.08, "text": " Think about that the next time you put your noise-canceling headphones in, and the world", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 300, 264, 958, 565, 291, 829, 428, 5658, 12, 66, 4463, 11031, 16278, 294, 11, 293, 264, 1002, 50590], "temp